  ('accelerator-90-degree-hop-to-stick', '90-Degree Hop to Stick', '{"slug":"accelerator-90-degree-hop-to-stick","name":"90-Degree Hop to Stick","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Landing orientation → diagonal control: Review the turning-jump landing and a separate diagonal slam without adding height, ball mass or test attempts.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Landing orientation → diagonal control: Review the turning-jump landing and a separate diagonal slam without adding height, ball mass or test attempts. Provide a second matched lower-body rotational-output observation with a simple bilateral base. Use a smaller turn instead if control requires it, but record it as a changed condition. Do not add height, distance or retries to chase a score.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “90-Degree Hop to Stick.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Landing orientation → diagonal control: Review the turning-jump landing and a separate diagonal slam without adding height, ball mass or test attempts.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls. The elastic stiffness plyometric rudiments placement