  ('accelerator-90-degree-hop-to-stick-two-foot-countermovement-execution', '90-Degree Hop to Stick — two-foot countermovement execution', '{"slug":"accelerator-90-degree-hop-to-stick-two-foot-countermovement-execution","name":"90-Degree Hop to Stick — two-foot countermovement execution","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Load → rotational output: Compare the single dip of the turning jump with the single compact preload of the ball throw; each load flows into one action.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Load → rotational output: Compare the single dip of the turning jump with the single compact preload of the ball throw; each load flows into one action. Express rapid leg-driven rotation using a countermovement, with a repeatable two-foot base. Land feet, knees and pelvis facing the same direction. Use a smaller 45° turn instead, with the same dose, if 90° cannot be completed before landing; record the changed angle. Do not screw the feet around after contact.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “90-Degree Hop to Stick — two-foot countermovement execution.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"ankle","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Load → rotational output: Compare the single dip of the tu