  ('accelerator-a-march', 'A-march', '{"slug":"accelerator-a-march","name":"A-march","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Introduces deliberate upright marching rhythm and single-leg organization before the faster skipping drills.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"Drive one knee up through a comfortable marching range while the opposite arm moves forward. Keep the stance side tall and the foot under the body. Place the lifted foot down under the hips, then switch sides. Travel forward with deliberate, even steps for 10 m.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “A-march.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Introduces deliberate upright marching rhythm and single-leg organization before the faster skipping drills.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not chase fatigue, force range, or continue through a loss of joint, trunk, landing, or balance control.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequirements":{"primary_joint_actions":["brace_patter