  ('accelerator-arm-action-drill-seated-fast-exchanges', 'Arm Action Drill — seated fast exchanges', '{"slug":"accelerator-arm-action-drill-seated-fast-exchanges","name":"Arm Action Drill — seated fast exchanges","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Practice quick opposing arm action while the torso stays organized, without adding another ankle-impact task. Sit tall on a fitted stable bench, feet on the floor, no backrest assistance. Move relaxed bent arms…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Practice quick opposing arm action while the torso stays organized, without adding another ankle-impact task. Sit tall on a fitted stable bench, feet on the floor, no backrest assistance. Move relaxed bent arms forward/backward from the shoulders within a comfortable sprint-like range. Hands do not cross the trunk or strike the seat; avoid shrugging or exaggerated rocking. Use the fastest relaxed exchanges that preserve posture; reduce speed/range if the trunk supplies the movement. This isolates arm action, not complete arm–leg timing.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Arm Action Drill — seated fast exchanges.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bench","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Practice quick oppo