  ('accelerator-arms-overhead-ankle-pogo-low-parallel-stance', 'Arms-Overhead Ankle Pogo — low, parallel stance', '{"slug":"accelerator-arms-overhead-ankle-pogo-low-parallel-stance","name":"Arms-Overhead Ankle Pogo — low, parallel stance","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Maintain quick ankle return and a stacked trunk while the arms remain in the upward-reach position. Hold arms comfortably overhead before the first contact; use small knee motion, low clearance and quiet synchronous…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Maintain quick ankle return and a stacked trunk while the arms remain in the upward-reach position. Hold arms comfortably overhead before the first contact; use small knee motion, low clearance and quiet synchronous feet. Do not swing the arms down to manufacture height, arch the back or shrug into discomfort. One linked transition per bout. Lower the arms/use the ordinary pogo replacement if the arm position disrupts foot rhythm or trunk control.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Arms-Overhead Ankle Pogo — low, parallel stance.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"ankle","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Maintain quick ankle return and a stacked trunk while the arms remain in the 