  ('accelerator-auditory-go-pre-chambered-thigh-whip', 'Auditory-go pre-chambered thigh whip', '{"slug":"accelerator-auditory-go-pre-chambered-thigh-whip","name":"Auditory-go pre-chambered thigh whip","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Release proximal rotation from a prepared leg position without anticipating the start.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Release proximal rotation from a prepared leg position without anticipating the start. Set a low bent-knee chamber on the named leg. Wait still for the coach go word, then make one short brisk roundhouse thigh sweep with the knee folded and support foot free to turn; reset fully. Vary the go timing modestly, without long fatiguing holds. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: a predictable countdown instead if waiting posture fails; keep the pre-cue hold at or below about 3 s. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Auditory-go pre-chambered thigh whip.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_outp