  ('accelerator-bear-position-shoulder-tap', 'Bear Position Shoulder Tap', '{"slug":"accelerator-bear-position-shoulder-tap","name":"Bear Position Shoulder Tap","family":"Shoulder, wrist, and hand-support resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"scapular_wrist_hand_support_resilience","slot":"accelerator_resilience_upper_support","cardSummary":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness. Maintain trunk position while support briefly shifts to one arm. Hands below shoulders, knees just clear of the floor. Slowly lift one hand to touch the opposite shoulder, replace it, then alternate; pelvis stays level. Take about 3 seconds each rep. Use knees on the floor instead if the pelvis sways; keep the same slow tap dose.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Bear Position Shoulder Tap.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","whyItGoesHere":"Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work. The scapular wrist hand support resilience placemen