  ('accelerator-bent-knee-counter-sweep-to-chamber', 'Bent-knee counter-sweep to chamber', '{"slug":"accelerator-bent-knee-counter-sweep-to-chamber","name":"Bent-knee counter-sweep to chamber","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Coordinate a short free-thigh loading reversal with hip-turn initiation.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Coordinate a short free-thigh loading reversal with hip-turn initiation. Hold the free knee folded below hip height, move the thigh a small distance outward/back under control, then reverse briskly into a low forward roundhouse chamber as the support foot releases. No knee extension or ballistic end-range stretch. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: a smaller counter-sweep or a still start instead if the pelvis tips or the knee is flung beyond control. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Bent-knee counter-sweep to chamber.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":