  ('accelerator-bent-over-sprint-start-parallel-feet-first-two-steps', 'Bent-Over Sprint Start — parallel feet, first two steps', '{"slug":"accelerator-bent-over-sprint-start-parallel-feet-first-two-steps","name":"Bent-Over Sprint Start — parallel feet, first two steps","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Main task: create the first push from a still hand-free hip hinge, then step forward into individual support. Feet parallel near hip width, knees softly bent, hips slightly back, trunk inclined with a comfortable spine…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main task: create the first push from a still hand-free hip hinge, then step forward into individual support. Feet parallel near hip width, knees softly bent, hips slightly back, trunk inclined with a comfortable spine and arms free. Fit the whole starting body inside 0–2 m. Settle 2 s, push and bring the selected foot through; no backward step, preliminary hop or fall from tall standing. Let the posture rise naturally rather than forcing an early upright position. First pair is controlled-fast to establish stopping; second is faster only while control remains.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Bent-Over Sprint Start — parallel feet, first two steps.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"locomote","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"k