  ('accelerator-bilateral-band-external-rotation-elbows-at-sides', 'Bilateral Band External Rotation — elbows at sides', '{"slug":"accelerator-bilateral-band-external-rotation-elbows-at-sides","name":"Bilateral Band External Rotation — elbows at sides","family":"Shoulder, wrist, and hand-support resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"scapular_wrist_hand_support_resilience","slot":"accelerator_resilience_upper_support","cardSummary":"Apply light shoulder-rotator loading while controlling the upper-arm position used in pressing and rowing. Hold an unanchored light band between hands; elbows near 90 degrees at the ribs. Rotate forearms outward for 2 seconds, hold 1 second, return for 2 seconds. Stop for wrist substitution, elbow drift or shoulder discomfort.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Keep this light support at ≥5 technical RIR. Apply light shoulder-rotator loading while controlling the upper-arm position used in pressing and rowing. Hold an unanchored light band between hands; elbows near 90 degrees at the ribs. Rotate forearms outward for 2 seconds, hold 1 second, return for 2 seconds. Stop for wrist substitution, elbow drift or shoulder discomfort. Use instead: a lighter band or smaller outward rotation at the same easy dose, with elbows at the ribs. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Bilateral Band External Rotation — elbows at sides.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","w