  ('accelerator-c-skip', 'C-skip', '{"slug":"accelerator-c-skip","name":"C-skip","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Adds the team’s coached backside recovery pattern while retaining the same upright, low-intensity skipping framework.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"Add a small skip as one heel recovers comfortably toward the same-side hip. Keep the thigh generally beneath the trunk rather than driving the knee far forward. Return the foot under the body and alternate sides with opposite arm action. Travel through the lane with a light, even rhythm.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “C-skip.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Adds the team’s coached backside recovery pattern while retaining the same upright, low-intensity skipping framework.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not chase fatigue, force range, or continue through a loss of joint, trunk, landing, or balance control.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequirements":{