  ('accelerator-cable-band-chop-standing-band-execution', 'Cable / Band Chop — standing band execution', '{"slug":"accelerator-cable-band-chop-standing-band-execution","name":"Cable / Band Chop — standing band execution","family":"Accessory and tissue capacity","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"tissue_capacity_isometric_eccentric_accessory","slot":"accelerator_capacity_accessory","cardSummary":"Load the downward diagonal arm path and its controlled return, supporting rotational hand acceleration and braking without adding another release.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Keep the working load at 2–3 technical reps/cycles in reserve. Load the downward diagonal arm path and its controlled return, supporting rotational hand acceleration and braking without adding another release. Secure a band at a verified high anchor to one side. Stand in a comfortable split stance with the opposite foot forward. With both hands, move from above the anchor-side shoulder toward the opposite front pocket while feet and hips turn through a modest arc. Drive in 1–2 seconds and return in 3 seconds. Keep the trunk long; avoid sideways crunching and band recoil. No cable machine is assumed. Use instead: Reduce band resistance or diagonal range if the athlete side-bends or loses control. If a suitable secure high anchor is unavailable, stop and re-audit the slot; do not improvise an unsafe anchor. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Cable / Band Chop — standing band execution.” Preser