  ('accelerator-cable-band-lift-standing-band-execution', 'Cable / Band Lift — standing band execution', '{"slug":"accelerator-cable-band-lift-standing-band-execution","name":"Cable / Band Lift — standing band execution","family":"Accessory and tissue capacity","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"tissue_capacity_isometric_eccentric_accessory","slot":"accelerator_capacity_accessory","cardSummary":"Load the low-to-high turning path from the hip to the hands and control its return, supporting the selected rising or scooping upper rotational action.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Keep the working load at 2–3 technical reps/cycles in reserve. Load the low-to-high turning path from the hip to the hands and control its return, supporting the selected rising or scooping upper rotational action. Secure a band at a verified low anchor behind one side. Stand in a comfortable split stance. Guide both hands from the rear hip across toward the opposite upper chest, allowing a small foot-and-hip turn. Drive in 1–2 seconds and return in 3 seconds. Keep ribs stacked and stop below any range that requires leaning back or shrugging. No cable machine is assumed. Use instead: Reduce resistance or range if the athlete leans back or loses a controlled return. If a suitable secure low anchor is unavailable, stop and re-audit the slot; do not improvise an unsafe anchor. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Cable / Band Lift — standing band execution.” Preserve its declared stance, dir