  ('accelerator-carioca-karaoke', 'Carioca / karaoke', '{"slug":"accelerator-carioca-karaoke","name":"Carioca / karaoke","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Adds controlled crossing steps and trunk-pelvis coordination after the simpler lateral shuffle has established side-to-side control.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"Step the trail foot behind the lead leg. Step laterally with the lead foot to reopen the base. Step the trail foot in front, then step laterally again with the lead foot. Repeat smoothly to the marker, stop under control and reverse direction.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Carioca / karaoke.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Adds controlled crossing steps and trunk-pelvis coordination after the simpler lateral shuffle has established side-to-side control.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not chase fatigue, force range, or continue through a loss of joint, trunk, landing, or balance control.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movemen