  ('accelerator-close-held-medicine-ball-rotational-snap-to-stop', 'Close-held medicine-ball rotational snap-to-stop', '{"slug":"accelerator-close-held-medicine-ball-rotational-snap-to-stop","name":"Close-held medicine-ball rotational snap-to-stop","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Brake the trunk-and-hands impulse without a release or catch.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Brake the trunk-and-hands impulse without a release or catch. Hold a very light ball close to the sternum. Make a short fast foot/hip/trunk turn, then stop the ball and body together within a comfortable arc for 2 seconds. Reset slowly; do not whip the ball at long arm length. Use instead: an unloaded palms-together turn instead if ball inertia prevents a clean stop. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Close-held medicine-ball rotational snap-to-stop.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"medicine_ball","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks