  ('accelerator-coach-called-leg-low-roundhouse', 'Coach-called-leg low roundhouse', '{"slug":"accelerator-coach-called-leg-low-roundhouse","name":"Coach-called-leg low roundhouse","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Directly link support-leg selection to the hip-led kick without an extra entry task.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Directly link support-leg selection to the hip-led kick without an extra entry task. Start from a still parallel athletic stance. The coach names the kicking leg before movement. Shift to the other leg, turn the support foot with the pelvis and perform a low roundhouse with active recoil and a controlled return. Complete the written side dose using the stated side-bout rest; vary the early call only within that schedule and never add calls or attempts. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a preannounced leg instead if the choice causes a rushed plant; cue accuracy never overrides safe mechanics. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Coach-called-leg low roundhouse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; r