  ('accelerator-countermovement-jump-rebound-one-linked-rebound', 'Countermovement Jump Rebound — one linked rebound', '{"slug":"accelerator-countermovement-jump-rebound-one-linked-rebound","name":"Countermovement Jump Rebound — one linked rebound","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Main task: accept a self-generated floor landing and redirect force upward. Start stationary on two feet with natural arms, make a controlled vertical CMJ, land on both feet and use one smooth yielding action for the…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main task: accept a self-generated floor landing and redirect force upward. Start stationary on two feet with natural arms, make a controlled vertical CMJ, land on both feet and use one smooth yielding action for the second jump. Land again on both feet, hold 2 s and reset. Keep both flights modest initially, with no obstacle or external drop. End after the first landing if symmetry/control is lost; do not force the rebound to finish a count. Reduce intent or use isolated jumps if pausing, deep collapse, knee loss, drift or an unwanted third jump appears.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Countermovement Jump Rebound — one linked rebound.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_region