  ('accelerator-countermovement-rotational-shot-put-throw', 'Countermovement rotational shot-put throw', '{"slug":"accelerator-countermovement-rotational-shot-put-throw","name":"Countermovement rotational shot-put throw","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Paused jump → countermovement push: Keep the jump free of a redip, then allow exactly one preload in the shot-put. Different starts are different tasks, not comparable power tests.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Paused jump → countermovement push: Keep the jump free of a redip, then allow exactly one preload in the shot-put. Different starts are different tasks, not comparable power tests. Apply prompt reversal to a unilateral pressing release. Ball supported beside the rear shoulder; allow one small backward body turn, then pivot forward and push toward the low target with the rear hand. Keep the elbow below shoulder height and guide hand relaxed. Reduce the preload or ball mass if the wrist collapses or the arm winds behind the torso. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Countermovement rotational shot-put throw.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"medicine_ball","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"P