  ('accelerator-crossover-entry-to-rotational-knee-chamber', 'Crossover entry to rotational knee chamber', '{"slug":"accelerator-crossover-entry-to-rotational-knee-chamber","name":"Crossover entry to rotational knee chamber","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Organize the hip turn after a crossover approach without adding another full kick dose.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Organize the hip turn after a crossover approach without adding another full kick dose. Take one short crossover travel step and then uncross onto the support foot; rotate with that foot while lifting the free bent knee into a low chamber. Put it down into stance after a 2 s finish. No kick extension or flight; the full entry fits inside 2 m. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: less crossing distance and a lower chamber instead if feet tangle; do not turn while the legs remain crossed. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Crossover entry to rotational knee chamber.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","we