  ('accelerator-crossover-recovery-to-a-marked-kick-base', 'Crossover recovery to a marked kick base', '{"slug":"accelerator-crossover-recovery-to-a-marked-kick-base","name":"Crossover recovery to a marked kick base","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Recover an exact useful two-foot base after reorientation, instead of leaving the feet crossed or too narrow.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Recover an exact useful two-foot base after reorientation, instead of leaving the feet crossed or too narrow. From a slightly open stance, take one short crossover recovery step, then uncross the feet as the pelvis turns into a premarked comfortable kick base. Stop for 2 s with both feet supporting. No knee lift, kick or jump; path stays within 2 m. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: less crossover distance and a wider base instead if foot placement is inconsistent; do not force a fast turn while crossed. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Crossover recovery to a marked kick base.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"me