  ('accelerator-dead-stop-kettlebell-swing-two-hands-one-float-per-reset', 'Dead-Stop Kettlebell Swing — two hands, one float per reset', '{"slug":"accelerator-dead-stop-kettlebell-swing-two-hands-one-float-per-reset","name":"Dead-Stop Kettlebell Swing — two hands, one float per reset","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Re-establish hip loading and a rapid drive for each initiation rather than relying on a continuous swing rhythm. With the bell parked just ahead within comfortable reach, hinge with a stable spine, grip with both hands,…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Re-establish hip loading and a rapid drive for each initiation rather than relying on a continuous swing rhythm. With the bell parked just ahead within comfortable reach, hinge with a stable spine, grip with both hands, hike it back once, drive the hips to a tall finish and let the bell float no higher than chest level. Guide its return through the hinge and park it under control before resetting. Feet remain planted; no arm lift, backward lean or release. Reduce bell size/load for a slow drive or unstable hike/park. This is a parked-single variant of the earlier swing family, not a swing without any backswing.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Dead-Stop Kettlebell Swing — two hands, one float per reset.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readines