  ('accelerator-dumbbell-hammer-curl-simultaneous-arms', 'Dumbbell Hammer Curl — simultaneous arms', '{"slug":"accelerator-dumbbell-hammer-curl-simultaneous-arms","name":"Dumbbell Hammer Curl — simultaneous arms","family":"Pull, hang, and grip strength","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"pull_hang_grip_strength","slot":"accelerator_capacity_pull","cardSummary":"Give elbow flexors direct loading for completing the draw in rows without another shoulder-extension set. Stand still, neutral grips, upper arms at sides; lift in 1 second, hold 1 second and lower for 2 seconds. No hip swing or wrist collapse. Both arms move together; this is 8 bilateral cycles, not 8 alternating reps.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Keep the working load at 2–3 technical reps/cycles in reserve. Give elbow flexors direct loading for completing the draw in rows without another shoulder-extension set. Stand still, neutral grips, upper arms at sides; lift in 1 second, hold 1 second and lower for 2 seconds. No hip swing or wrist collapse. Both arms move together; this is 8 bilateral cycles, not 8 alternating reps. Use instead: lighter dumbbells with the same simultaneous neutral-grip curl and controlled range. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Dumbbell Hammer Curl — simultaneous arms.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Own the position and finish every rep with two or three good reps still available.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"strength","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"resistance_calisthenics","weight":5}],"physio