  ('accelerator-dumbbell-high-hang-pull-no-flight-or-catch', 'Dumbbell High-Hang Pull — no flight or catch', '{"slug":"accelerator-dumbbell-high-hang-pull-no-flight-or-catch","name":"Dumbbell High-Hang Pull — no flight or catch","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Accelerate a small external load upward through coordinated knee/hip extension and heel rise. Begin tall, dumbbells beside the thighs, arms long; make a shallow dip/hinge to high-thigh level, then drive tall quickly…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Accelerate a small external load upward through coordinated knee/hip extension and heel rise. Begin tall, dumbbells beside the thighs, arms long; make a shallow dip/hinge to high-thigh level, then drive tall quickly onto the forefeet. Allow a natural shoulder rise, keep elbows long and weights close; no deliberate high elbow pull, rack catch, jump or backward lean. Lower under control over about 2 s, heels down, reset. Choose a load permitting crisp leg-driven motion; first three reps establish technique conservatively. Reduce load/intent or stop for arm hauling, lost trunk position or uncontrolled lowering.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Dumbbell High-Hang Pull — no flight or catch.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"pull","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"dumb