  ('accelerator-early-point-rotational-jump-to-stick', 'Early-point rotational jump to stick', '{"slug":"accelerator-early-point-rotational-jump-to-stick","name":"Early-point rotational jump to stick","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Called landing → diagonal stop: Choose the jump direction before takeoff and own the landing; separately stop a single diagonal rope pulse from a planned stance.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Called landing → diagonal stop: Choose the jump direction before takeoff and own the landing; separately stop a single diagonal rope pulse from a planned stance. Commit a turn direction before takeoff and preserve landing organization despite a decision demand. Use an announced smaller turn instead if the athlete starts early or cannot land facing the intended line.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Early-point rotational jump to stick.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Called landing → diagonal stop: Choose the jump direction before takeoff and own the landing; separately stop a single diagonal rope pulse from a planned stance.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output qualit