  ('accelerator-externally-supplied-rotational-scoop-return', 'Externally supplied rotational scoop return', '{"slug":"accelerator-externally-supplied-rotational-scoop-return","name":"Externally supplied rotational scoop return","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Organize a supplied ball into a balanced rotational release.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Organize a supplied ball into a balanced rotational release. While the athlete is stationary, the coach places a light ball securely into both hands near the rear hip. After the coach fully releases and clears the motion and release path, establish grip, turn feet, hips and trunk, then make a low forward scoop release. This combined execution uses a controlled handoff only, with no airborne feed or rebound catch. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Use instead: a self-held paused rotational scoop instead if a safe handoff, secure grip, feeder clearance or balanced turn cannot be qualified; this replacement has no ball reception. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Externally supplied rotational scoop return.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","ath