  ('accelerator-externally-supplied-rotational-shot-put-return', 'Externally supplied rotational shot-put return', '{"slug":"accelerator-externally-supplied-rotational-shot-put-return","name":"Externally supplied rotational shot-put return","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Land and organize → push return: Use the source bounce-to-kick gate, then organize a handoff before the shot-put. Hold the landing or self-hold the ball when readiness requires.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Land and organize → push return: Use the source bounce-to-kick gate, then organize a handoff before the shot-put. Hold the landing or self-hold the ball when readiness requires. Transfer reception at the chest into unilateral pressing. Receive a handoff in both hands near the rear chest. Once supported securely, guide with the front hand, pivot and push with the rear hand toward the low target. A verified gentle feed replaces the handoff only under the stated gate. Use the self-held standing shot-put instead if grip or wrist alignment fails. Rest 90 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Externally supplied rotational shot-put return.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"medicine_ball","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"k