  ('accelerator-floor-press-alternating-light-speed-presses-opposite-arm-parked', 'Floor Press — alternating light speed presses, opposite arm parked', '{"slug":"accelerator-floor-press-alternating-light-speed-presses-opposite-arm-parked","name":"Floor Press — alternating light speed presses, opposite arm parked","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Coordinate alternating forward arm force while retaining control of the other load. Both dumbbells start with upper arms gently on floor. Press one arm quickly while the other remains parked at the floor boundary, lower…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Coordinate alternating forward arm force while retaining control of the other load. Both dumbbells start with upper arms gently on floor. Press one arm quickly while the other remains parked at the floor boundary, lower 2 s, then switch; four total presses, two per arm. No simultaneous lift, torso roll or weight release. Reset 5 s between reps. Use two simultaneous bilateral light floor-press cycles if alternating load handling is unsuitable; record changed cycle counting instead of this slot if the stated execution is unsuitable; follow any explicitly stated replacement dose; otherwise retain the remaining dose. Log changed laterality/exposure; stop if control cannot be restored.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Floor Press — alternating light speed presses, opposite arm parked.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosivenes