  ('accelerator-forward-plant-and-open-to-kick-stance', 'Forward plant-and-open to kick stance', '{"slug":"accelerator-forward-plant-and-open-to-kick-stance","name":"Forward plant-and-open to kick stance","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Accept forward arrival onto a leg before freeing the other thigh for a kick.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Accept forward arrival onto a leg before freeing the other thigh for a kick. Take one brisk short forward step onto the receiving leg and open the feet/pelvis into a shallow split kick stance, no more than 45 degrees from the initial facing. Keep the step and finish inside 2 m; no kick or run-up. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: Shorten the step if the athlete overstrides, stiffens the knee or drags a planted foot through the turn. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Forward plant-and-open to kick stance.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key"