  ('accelerator-forward-step-diagonal-medicine-ball-side-slam', 'Forward-step diagonal medicine-ball side slam', '{"slug":"accelerator-forward-step-diagonal-medicine-ball-side-slam","name":"Forward-step diagonal medicine-ball side slam","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Drop-step takeoff → forward diagonal: Control the loaded turning jump, then organize a separate forward step and diagonal slam with a stable endpoint.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Drop-step takeoff → forward diagonal: Control the loaded turning jump, then organize a separate forward step and diagonal slam with a stable endpoint. Arrest forward entry and deliver force downward through the turn. With ball at upper-chest height, take one small lead-foot step, plant and turn into a diagonal slam slightly forward/outside that foot. No overhead circle or jump. Use the stationary shoulder-height side slam instead if the foot cannot plant before the hands drive. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Forward-step diagonal medicine-ball side slam.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"push","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"slam_ball","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Drop-step takeoff → forward diagonal: Control the loaded turning jump, then organize a separate forward step and diagonal slam with a stable endpoint.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls. The jump throw explosive power placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not shorten recovery, add fatigue reps, or continue after speed, landing, direction, or release quality declines.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequirements":{"primary_joint_actions":["push_pattern_control"],"primary_tissues":["shoulder"],"primary_motor_control_demands":["jump_throw_explosive_power"],"breathing_demand":"continuous breathing without bracing or breath-holding drift","balance_demand":"moderate","coordination_demand":"moderate","impact_level":1},"coachingExecution":{"movement_description":"Drop-step takeoff → forward diagonal: Control the loaded turning jump, then organize a separate forward step and diagonal slam with a stable endpoint. Arrest forward entry and deliver force downward through the turn. With ball at upper-chest height, take one small lead-foot step, plant and turn into a diagonal slam slightly forward/outside that foot. No overhead circle or jump. Use the stationary shoulder-height side slam instead if the foot cannot plant before the hands drive. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","setup":["Prepare Slam ball, Marked space; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Drop-step takeoff → forward diagonal: Control the loaded turning jump, then organize a separate forward step and diagonal slam with a stable endpoint."],"execution_steps":["Drop-step takeoff → forward diagonal: Control the loaded turning jump, then organize a separate forward step and diagonal slam with a stable endpoint.","Arrest forward entry and deliver force downward through the turn."