  ('accelerator-forward-step-in-low-roundhouse', 'Forward step-in low roundhouse', '{"slug":"accelerator-forward-step-in-low-roundhouse","name":"Forward step-in low roundhouse","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Directly translate controlled forward arrival into pelvic rotation and free-leg acceleration.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Directly translate controlled forward arrival into pelvic rotation and free-leg acceleration. With the kicking leg initially rear, step the support foot a short distance forward, accept weight with a soft knee, let that foot turn and launch the low rear-leg roundhouse. Recoil and recover within the same 2 m work segment. No run-up or pad. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a shorter/slower step instead for overstriding or extra braking steps; preserve controlled brisk kick intent after the qualified plant. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Forward step-in low roundhouse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key"