  ('accelerator-grounded-snap-down-to-forward-rebound-jump', 'Grounded Snap-Down to Forward Rebound Jump', '{"slug":"accelerator-grounded-snap-down-to-forward-rebound-jump","name":"Grounded Snap-Down to Forward Rebound Jump","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Create a quick active lowering action and use it for forward force. Start tall with arms raised and heels lightly lifted; snap into a shallow athletic position without leaving the floor, then immediately jump forward…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Create a quick active lowering action and use it for forward force. Start tall with arms raised and heels lightly lifted; snap into a shallow athletic position without leaving the floor, then immediately jump forward and hold the final landing. Regress/stop: Reduce lowering speed/depth and travel; stop if an unintended initial hop appears or the athlete loses the foot base.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Grounded Snap-Down to Forward Rebound Jump.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Create a quick active lowering action and use it for forward force. Start tall with arms raised and heels lightly lifted; snap into a shallow athletic position without leav