  ('accelerator-grounded-snap-down-to-low-rebound-jump', 'Grounded Snap-Down to Low Rebound Jump', '{"slug":"accelerator-grounded-snap-down-to-low-rebound-jump","name":"Grounded Snap-Down to Low Rebound Jump","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Organize a rapid lowering into a responsive push without adding the energy of a drop from a box. Start tall with heels lightly raised but forefeet grounded; quickly settle heels and bend hips/knees slightly, then make…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Organize a rapid lowering into a responsive push without adding the energy of a drop from a box. Start tall with heels lightly raised but forefeet grounded; quickly settle heels and bend hips/knees slightly, then make one small vertical rebound jump and stick 2 s. The initial snap-down has no flight. Reduce speed/depth if alignment is lost; no extra pogo afterward.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Grounded Snap-Down to Low Rebound Jump.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Organize a rapid lowering into a responsive push without adding the energy of a drop from a box. Start tall with heels lightly raised but forefeet grounded; quickly settle heels and bend hips/knees sli