  ('accelerator-grounded-switch-step-rotational-knee-drive', 'Grounded switch-step rotational knee drive', '{"slug":"accelerator-grounded-switch-step-rotational-knee-drive","name":"Grounded switch-step rotational knee drive","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Link a fast support-role exchange to proximal rotational output without a full additional kick.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Link a fast support-role exchange to proximal rotational output without a full additional kick. Exchange front/rear foot positions with two short grounded steps, let the new support foot settle and turn, and drive the free folded knee across into a low rotational chamber. No hop, knee extension or contact; finish within 2 m. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: slower, shorter exchange steps instead until the legs uncross cleanly; never pivot while the feet are tangled. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Grounded switch-step rotational knee drive.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}]