  ('accelerator-half-kneeling-get-up-to-stand-rapid-lead-leg-drive', 'Half-Kneeling Get-Up to Stand — rapid lead-leg drive', '{"slug":"accelerator-half-kneeling-get-up-to-stand-rapid-lead-leg-drive","name":"Half-Kneeling Get-Up to Stand — rapid lead-leg drive","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Express upward force from greater front-leg flexion with a supported starting position. Start with the lead whole foot flat and rear knee on a comfortable floor, torso organized over the lead foot. Drive through the…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Express upward force from greater front-leg flexion with a supported starting position. Start with the lead whole foot flat and rear knee on a comfortable floor, torso organized over the lead foot. Drive through the lead leg to stand; let the rear leg follow into a knee lift, without jumping or pushing hands on the thigh. Rear toes may assist the initial transition; do not claim a pure one-leg force measure. Use secure light hand support if balance limits drive. If it remains slow/grinding or knee contact is uncomfortable, use the shallower standing replacement below.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Half-Kneeling Get-Up to Stand — rapid lead-leg drive.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none