m greater front-leg flexion with a supported starting position.","Start with the lead whole foot flat and rear knee on a comfortable floor, torso organized over the lead foot.","Drive through the lead leg to stand; let the rear leg follow into a knee lift, without jumping or pushing hands on the thigh.","Rear toes may assist the initial transition; do not claim a pure one-leg force measure.","Complete 1 × 3 per lead leg = 6 non-flight rises. Rise briskly, hold the free knee up briefly, then lower over about 3 s to the same half-kneeling start. 20 s between same-lead efforts; 60 s between leads; 90 s before E5.; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"reps","default_sets":1,"default_reps":3,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":90,"est_seconds_per_set":45,"default_rpe_min":7,"default_rpe_max":9},"scaling":{"youth_beginner":"Reduce load, range, speed, distance, impact, and decision demand. Use one coached rep at a time and stop at the first loss of control.","youth_intermediate":"Use the written pattern at a conservative dose; progress one variable only after repeated clean sessions.","teen":"Use the class prescription when readiness and technique support it; keep full recovery for explosive work and clean reps in