  ('accelerator-half-kneeling-rotational-med-ball-throw-floor-target-adaptation', 'Half-Kneeling Rotational Med Ball Throw — floor-target adaptation', '{"slug":"accelerator-half-kneeling-rotational-med-ball-throw-floor-target-adaptation","name":"Half-Kneeling Rotational Med Ball Throw — floor-target adaptation","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Express trunk-to-hand acceleration with leg propulsion reduced.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Express trunk-to-hand acceleration with leg propulsion reduced. Set the target-side foot forward with the opposite knee comfortably supported on the floor. Begin the light ball beside the rear hip. Use a small comfortable thoracic turn and fast two-hand release toward the low target. Keep the front foot planted and pelvis quiet without forcing a rigid pelvis through a larger trunk twist. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Use instead: Shorten the turn or use a lighter ball if the knee shifts or back arches. If kneeling contact is intolerable, use a seated bench rotational throw with a small comfortable trunk turn instead. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Half-Kneeling Rotational Med Ball Throw — floor-target adaptation.” Preserve its declared