ll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Use instead: Shorten the turn or use a lighter ball if the knee shifts or back arches. If kneeling contact is intolerable, use a seated bench rotational throw with a small comfortable trunk turn instead. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","setup":["Prepare Medicine ball, Verified contained throwing area, Comfortable floor contact; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Express trunk-to-hand acceleration with leg propulsion reduced."],"execution_steps":["Express trunk-to-hand acceleration with leg propulsion reduced.","Set the target-side foot forward with the opposite knee comfortably supported on the floor.","Begin the light ball beside the rear hip.","Use a small comfortable thoracic turn and fast two-hand release toward the low target.","Complete 1 × 2 per side/direction; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"reps","default_sets":1,"default_reps":2,"default_work_secon