  ('accelerator-half-kneeling-sprint-start-first-two-steps', 'Half-Kneeling Sprint Start — first two steps', '{"slug":"accelerator-half-kneeling-sprint-start-first-two-steps","name":"Half-Kneeling Sprint Start — first two steps","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Main low-start task: create forward motion from a flexed lead hip/knee while bringing the rear thigh through. Front foot flat, rear knee comfortably supported on the floor and rear toes tucked; establish a modest…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main low-start task: create forward motion from a flexed lead hip/knee while bringing the rear thigh through. Front foot flat, rear knee comfortably supported on the floor and rear toes tucked; establish a modest forward torso lean without rounding, pause briefly, then push into the lane. Both legs may contribute; this is not a test of isolated lead-leg force. First pair uses controlled fast intent to establish the route; second pair uses the fastest clean intent that preserves stopping control.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Half-Kneeling Sprint Start — first two steps.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"locomote","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Main low-start task: create forward motion from