 tucked; establish a modest forward torso lean without rounding, pause briefly, then push into the lane.","Both legs may contribute; this is not a test of isolated lead-leg force.","First pair uses controlled fast intent to establish the route; second pair uses the fastest clean intent that preserves stopping control.","Complete 2 × 2 starts, one with each front leg per pair. Front toes at 1 m; fit the entire starting body inside 0–2 m. At most 2 driving strikes or 3 m of drive, ending by 4 m; progressively slow and stop by 9 m. 75 s between starts; 120 s between pairs.; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"distance","default_sets":2,"default_reps":2,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":90,"est_seconds_per_set":45,"default_rpe_min":7,"default_rpe_max":9},"scaling":{"youth_beginner":"Reduce load, range, speed, distance, impact, and decision demand. Use one coached rep at a time and stop at the first loss of control.","youth_intermediate":"Use the written pattern at a conservative dose; progress one variable only after repeated clean sessions.","teen":"Use the class prescription when readiness and technique support it; keep full recovery for explosive work and clean reps in reserve for strength.","adult_beginn