  ('accelerator-hamstring-walkout-complete-out-and-back-cycle', 'Hamstring Walkout — complete out-and-back cycle', '{"slug":"accelerator-hamstring-walkout-complete-out-and-back-cycle","name":"Hamstring Walkout — complete out-and-back cycle","family":"Hinge and posterior-chain strength","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"hinge_posterior_chain_strength","slot":"accelerator_capacity_hinge","cardSummary":"Knee-flexor leverage while the pelvis stays raised, distinct from moving through a hip hinge. Start in a bilateral bridge. Each cycle is two small heel steps out per foot, then two back per foot: eight placements in…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Knee-flexor leverage while the pelvis stays raised, distinct from moving through a hip hinge. Start in a bilateral bridge. Each cycle is two small heel steps out per foot, then two back per foot: eight placements in about 8 s. Keep a soft knee and level hips; never chase a fully straight leg. Recovery: No additional set is prescribed; finish this exercise without bonus work. Use instead: a shorter-lever walkout at the same complete-cycle count; reduce range for sagging or cramp and stop if control does not return. This replaces remaining work in this slot; follow an explicit replacement dose if stated, otherwise keep the remaining dose/rest. Log changed events or laterality.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Hamstring Walkout — complete out-and-back cycle.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Own the position and finish every rep with two or three good reps still available.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"strength","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"resistance_calisthenics","weight":5}],"