  ('accelerator-handoff-to-step-rotational-medicine-ball-scoop-return', 'Handoff-to-step rotational medicine-ball scoop return', '{"slug":"accelerator-handoff-to-step-rotational-medicine-ball-scoop-return","name":"Handoff-to-step rotational medicine-ball scoop return","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Establish grip, plant a deliberate step, then project through rotation.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Establish grip, plant a deliberate step, then project through rotation. Receive the coach’s handoff near the rear hip while stationary. After the coach fully releases and steps clear, take one small lead-foot step, plant, pivot and scoop toward the low target; hold the finish. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Keep all entry and finish footwork inside a cleared 1-metre start bay; no hop, jump or sprint. Use instead: the self-held step-in scoop instead if handoff timing or feeder clearance is unreliable. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Handoff-to-step rotational medicine-ball scoop return.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully befo