  ('accelerator-hip-thrust-bench-supported-rapid-rise', 'Hip Thrust — bench-supported rapid rise', '{"slug":"accelerator-hip-thrust-bench-supported-rapid-rise","name":"Hip Thrust — bench-supported rapid rise","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Express hip extension through the finish with shoulder support allowing a different range from the floor bridge. Use bodyweight first. Support the upper back, not the neck, on a low stable bench that cannot slide; feet…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Express hip extension through the finish with shoulder support allowing a different range from the floor bridge. Use bodyweight first. Support the upper back, not the neck, on a low stable bench that cannot slide; feet flat and knees comfortable. Lower 2 s, drive hips up quickly and hold 1 s with ribs and pelvis aligned. No lumbar arch or head throw. Recovery: 10 s between individual reps; 90 s before the next exercise/section Use instead: three rapid floor-bridge rises with the same reset/rest if bench height, friction or shoulder support is unsuitable. This replaces remaining work in this slot; follow an explicit replacement dose if stated, otherwise keep the remaining dose/rest. Log changed events or laterality.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Hip Thrust — bench-supported rapid rise.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_r