  ('accelerator-inchworm-plank-bear-crawl-downward-dog', 'Inchworm → plank → bear crawl → downward dog', '{"slug":"accelerator-inchworm-plank-bear-crawl-downward-dog","name":"Inchworm → plank → bear crawl → downward dog","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Combines controlled fold, hand support, trunk organization, contralateral travel and a comfortable posterior-chain position in one low-speed sequence.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"From standing, soften the knees as needed and walk the hands forward into a controlled plank. Hold the plank briefly with hands under the shoulders and the trunk organized. Take small bear-crawl steps with opposite hand and foot moving without rushing. Press the hips up and back into a comfortable downward-dog shape. Walk the feet toward the hands, stand with control and repeat to 10 m.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Inchworm → plank → bear crawl → downward dog.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"locomote","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"core","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Combines controlled fold, hand support, trunk organization, contralateral travel and a comfortable posterior-chain position in one low-speed sequence.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominan