  ('accelerator-lateral-bound-to-rotational-stick', 'Lateral Bound to Rotational Stick', '{"slug":"accelerator-lateral-bound-to-rotational-stick","name":"Lateral Bound to Rotational Stick","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Absorb → diagonal force: Own the rotational bound landing, then use a settled base to direct the side slam. The landing and slam are separate efforts with full recovery.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Absorb → diagonal force: Own the rotational bound landing, then use a settled base to direct the side slam. The landing and slam are separate efforts with full recovery. Load the single-leg lateral plant that must accept the body before a hip turn. The turn occurs during flight; no twisting on touchdown. Choose distance inside a cleared 2 m travel segment and permit a separate clear 2 m recovery area. Shorten the bound/turn for pelvic drop or a recovery hop. If turn clearance/control is insufficient, use instead a short lateral bound to stick without the turn, same dose; retain a clear landing/recovery area.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lateral Bound to Rotational Stick.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Absorb → diagonal force