  ('accelerator-lateral-lunge-reach', 'Lateral lunge + reach', '{"slug":"accelerator-lateral-lunge-reach","name":"Lateral lunge + reach","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Accesses a supported side-to-side stance and links lateral hip loading with a controlled reach before ground-based locomotion.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"Step laterally and sit the hips toward the stepping side through a comfortable range. Keep the stepping foot supported while the opposite leg remains long but not forced. Reach forward or toward the stepping foot without losing the base. Return to tall, bring the feet together and repeat while traveling.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lateral lunge + reach.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"squat","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Accesses a supported side-to-side stance and links lateral hip loading with a controlled reach before ground-based locomotion.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not chase fatigue, force range, or continue through a loss of joint, trunk, landing, or balance control.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance