  ('accelerator-lateral-release-step-from-held-split-stance', 'Lateral release step from held split stance', '{"slug":"accelerator-lateral-release-step-from-held-split-stance","name":"Lateral release step from held split stance","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Release planted leg force into a grounded turn when there is no incoming momentum.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Release planted leg force into a grounded turn when there is no incoming momentum. Hold a shallow split stance for 2 s with the named leg in front. Push from that leg into one short lateral step, allow the feet/pelvis to open together up to 45 degrees, and finish in a stable kick stance. No jump or follow-on kick. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: Shorten the step and turn for foot sticking or overstriding; keep motion within 2 m. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lateral release step from held split stance.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readines