  ('accelerator-lateral-shuffle', 'Lateral shuffle', '{"slug":"accelerator-lateral-shuffle","name":"Lateral shuffle","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Adds controlled side-to-side travel and exposes both directions before more complex transverse-plane movement.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"Lower into a comfortable athletic stance. Push the floor away with the trail leg and step laterally with the lead leg. Bring the trail foot back under the body without crossing the feet. Stay square, stop under control, then repeat in the opposite direction.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lateral shuffle.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"locomote","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Adds controlled side-to-side travel and exposes both directions before more complex transverse-plane movement.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not chase fatigue, force range, or continue through a loss of joint, trunk, landing, or balance control.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequiremen