  ('accelerator-lateral-step-in-to-rotational-plant', 'Lateral step-in to rotational plant', '{"slug":"accelerator-lateral-step-in-to-rotational-plant","name":"Lateral step-in to rotational plant","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Convert arriving lateral bodyweight into a grounded foot-and-hip turn with a controlled split-stance finish.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Convert arriving lateral bodyweight into a grounded foot-and-hip turn with a controlled split-stance finish. From a parallel athletic stance, take one brisk short lateral step onto the receiving foot, then turn the feet and pelvis together up to 45 degrees into a shallow split kick stance. Let the receiving heel release and the other foot realign. Hold the finish for 2 seconds. Keep the step and finish within 2 metres, with another 2 metres clear for recovery. No kick, run-up or flight. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: Shorten the step and turn angle if the athlete overstrides, shuffles again or traps the knee. Both feet must be able to realign with the pelvis. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lateral step-in to rotational plant.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort 