  ('accelerator-lateral-step-transverse-battle-rope-pulse', 'Lateral-step transverse battle-rope pulse', '{"slug":"accelerator-lateral-step-transverse-battle-rope-pulse","name":"Lateral-step transverse battle-rope pulse","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Adductor contribution → lateral hand pulse: Control the rapid short-lever adduction, then coordinate that lateral support demand with a grounded step and transverse rope pulse.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Adductor contribution → lateral hand pulse: Control the rapid short-lever adduction, then coordinate that lateral support demand with a grounded step and transverse rope pulse. Transfer a small lateral arrival into a retained inertial sweep. With rope settled, step laterally a short distance, plant and sweep both rope ends toward the opposite hip using a small body turn. Settle completely before returning to the start. Use the stationary transverse whip instead if entry clearance or placement is inadequate. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lateral-step transverse battle-rope pulse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"battle_rope","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Adductor contribution → lateral ha