  ('accelerator-lateral-step-two-hand-medicine-ball-backhand-throw', 'Lateral-step two-hand medicine-ball backhand throw', '{"slug":"accelerator-lateral-step-two-hand-medicine-ball-backhand-throw","name":"Lateral-step two-hand medicine-ball backhand throw","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Connect lateral arrival to an outward upper-body release.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Connect lateral arrival to an outward upper-body release. Start the ball across the lower ribs; take one short uncrossed lateral step toward the lane, plant, turn and sweep both hands outward into the low target. Hold the finish. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Keep all entry and finish footwork inside a cleared 1-metre start bay; no hop, jump or sprint. Use instead: the stationary backhand throw instead at this dose if arrival causes drift or the shoulder trails behind the trunk. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lateral-step two-hand medicine-ball backhand throw.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":