  ('accelerator-lead-hand-rotational-medicine-ball-push-throw', 'Lead-hand rotational medicine-ball push throw', '{"slug":"accelerator-lead-hand-rotational-medicine-ball-push-throw","name":"Lead-hand rotational medicine-ball push throw","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Express force through the arm nearest the target without a large rear-arm wind-up.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Express force through the arm nearest the target without a large rear-arm wind-up. Use a very light ball held at the lead-side chest with the other hand assisting its support. Make a small turn toward the lane and extend the lead arm into the low target; the supporting hand releases. Keep both feet planted/pivoting. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Use instead: a smaller grippable ball or shorten the turn if the lead shoulder rolls forward. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lead-hand rotational medicine-ball push throw.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"meth