  ('accelerator-lead-leg-low-roundhouse-without-a-gather-step', 'Lead-leg low roundhouse without a gather step', '{"slug":"accelerator-lead-leg-low-roundhouse-without-a-gather-step","name":"Lead-leg low roundhouse without a gather step","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Directly train front-leg release while the rear leg supplies the rotational base.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Directly train front-leg release while the rear leg supplies the rotational base. Start with the kicking leg in front. Shift onto the rear support leg, allow its foot to pivot, then execute one low roundhouse with a soft terminal knee, active recoil and a return to the starting stance. Do not shuffle the rear foot forward first. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a lower chamber/shorter extension instead if the athlete needs an extra gather or leans away; do not speed up a trapped rear-foot pivot. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Lead-leg low roundhouse without a gather step.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.