  ('accelerator-light-band-pallof-press-fixed-split-stance', 'Light-Band Pallof Press — fixed split stance', '{"slug":"accelerator-light-band-pallof-press-fixed-split-stance","name":"Light-Band Pallof Press — fixed split stance","family":"Trunk and pelvic resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"trunk_pelvis_anti_movement_control","slot":"accelerator_resilience_trunk","cardSummary":"Control unwanted trunk rotation while force passes through a planted lead foot. Rated side attachment at chest height, light tension. Press hands forward 1 s, hold 2 s, return 2 s without rotating; change anchor-facing…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Control unwanted trunk rotation while force passes through a planted lead foot. Rated side attachment at chest height, light tension. Press hands forward 1 s, hold 2 s, return 2 s without rotating; change anchor-facing side after rest. Complete one anchor side side, rest 30 s, then the other; 10 total reps. Use a light single-arm supine dumbbell press hold for 1 × 5 repetitions with a 2 s top hold per arm if no side attachment is available; record changed support instead of this slot if the stated execution is unsuitable; follow any explicitly stated replacement dose; otherwise retain the remaining dose. Log changed laterality/exposure; stop if control cannot be restored.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Light-Band Pallof Press — fixed split stance.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stabili