  ('accelerator-loaded-cossack-squat-goblet-dumbbell-qualified-depth', 'Loaded Cossack Squat — goblet dumbbell, qualified depth', '{"slug":"accelerator-loaded-cossack-squat-goblet-dumbbell-qualified-depth","name":"Loaded Cossack Squat — goblet dumbbell, qualified depth","family":"Squat and knee-dominant strength","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"squat_knee_dominant_strength","slot":"accelerator_capacity_squat","cardSummary":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern. Supply lateral hip/adductor force through a controlled range for the plant and sweeping-leg recovery. Distinct from the fore–aft split squat; one set per side limits overlap with E3. Keep the loaded foot supported and knee aligned; reduce depth/load for groin pulling or pelvic collapse. Deep range is not mandatory.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Loaded Cossack Squat — goblet dumbbell, qualified depth.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Own the position and finish every rep with two or three good reps still available.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"strength","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"resistance_calisthenics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"force_tissue_capacity","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"squat","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"dumbbell","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern.","whyItGoesHere":"Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropria