  ('accelerator-low-alternating-split-stance-pogo-two-switches-then-stop', 'Low Alternating Split-Stance Pogo — two switches then stop', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-alternating-split-stance-pogo-two-switches-then-stop","name":"Low Alternating Split-Stance Pogo — two switches then stop","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Practice quick ankle return while exchanging the fore/aft foot relationship, supporting precise foot placement before vertical drive. Use a very small stagger, small knee motion and low clearance; switch front/back…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Practice quick ankle return while exchanging the fore/aft foot relationship, supporting precise foot placement before vertical drive. Use a very small stagger, small knee motion and low clearance; switch front/back without crossing the feet across the body''s midline. Both feet leave and meet the floor together. Each bout has one linked transition and finishes with a 2 s split landing hold. No high lunge jump, deep split, tuck or speed chase. Use parallel low pogos if contacts become heavy, uneven or tangled.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low Alternating Split-Stance Pogo — two switches then stop.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[