  ('accelerator-low-bent-knee-hook-shadow-sweep', 'Low bent-knee hook shadow sweep', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-bent-knee-hook-shadow-sweep","name":"Low bent-knee hook shadow sweep","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Practice the coupled inward thigh sweep and knee folding used to recover a rotational leg action.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Practice the coupled inward thigh sweep and knee folding used to recover a rotational leg action. From a comfortable open kick stance, lift the free thigh low, extend only slightly and sweep inward while folding the knee, then place the foot under control. Keep the arc small, below hip height, and coordinate the support-foot turn; no spin or contact. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: an entirely folded-knee inward hook instead if the longer lever cannot be controlled; stop for groin or knee discomfort. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low bent-knee hook shadow sweep.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[