  ('accelerator-low-box-hip-switch-same-free-foot-tap-and-return', 'Low Box Hip Switch — same free-foot tap and return', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-box-hip-switch-same-free-foot-tap-and-return","name":"Low Box Hip Switch — same free-foot tap and return","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Maintain a level pelvis as the free foot moves between a raised-knee position and a lower contact surface. Keep the entire support foot on a stable platform approximately 10 cm high; begin with the other thigh…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Maintain a level pelvis as the free foot moves between a raised-knee position and a lower contact surface. Keep the entire support foot on a stable platform approximately 10 cm high; begin with the other thigh comfortably raised. Quickly lower that free foot to a light floor touch beside the platform and return the knee, allowing a small support-knee bend as needed. Switch the arms with the free leg. The support foot stays on the platform: this is not a jumping box exchange or a step-up. Reduce knee range/speed for a hip hitch, forceful floor push or trunk tilt.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low Box Hip Switch — same free-foot tap and return.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight