  ('accelerator-low-forward-pogos-two-hops-final-stick', 'Low Forward Pogos — two hops, final stick', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-forward-pogos-two-hops-final-stick","name":"Low Forward Pogos — two hops, final stick","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Retain a tall body while the ankles contribute a small forward push and reuse the first contact, linking ankle support to propulsion. Start with parallel feet at line 1 m, finish by line 2 m, and keep the entire 0–4 m…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Retain a tall body while the ankles contribute a small forward push and reuse the first contact, linking ankle support to propulsion. Start with parallel feet at line 1 m, finish by line 2 m, and keep the entire 0–4 m area clear for setup and any adjustment. Both feet leave/land together; no deep squat, long bound or chase for distance. Do not take the second hop if the first receiver is unstable or requires a deep recovery bend.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low Forward Pogos — two hops, final stick.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"ankle","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Retain a tall body while the ankles contribute a small forward push and reuse the first contact, linking ankle support to p