  ('accelerator-low-inward-crescent-shadow-sweep', 'Low inward crescent shadow sweep', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-inward-crescent-shadow-sweep","name":"Low inward crescent shadow sweep","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Express an inward thigh/adductor sweep that helps recover the leg after rotational extension.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Express an inward thigh/adductor sweep that helps recover the leg after rotational extension. With a soft knee, sweep the low free foot from slightly outside toward the midline in a small inward arc, coordinated with a comfortable support-foot/pelvic turn. Finish by folding the knee and placing the foot down. No crossing beyond a controllable midline range. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a bent-knee inward sweep instead at the same dose if the longer lever pulls at the groin; never force a high or locked-knee crescent. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low inward crescent shadow sweep.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"i