  ('accelerator-low-roundhouse-from-a-held-split-squat-start', 'Low roundhouse from a held split-squat start', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-roundhouse-from-a-held-split-squat-start","name":"Low roundhouse from a held split-squat start","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Link stance-leg force from stillness to the free thigh and pelvic turn.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Link stance-leg force from stillness to the free thigh and pelvic turn. Kicking leg starts rear. Hold a shallow split squat 2 s, then drive through the front support leg into a low roundhouse, actively recoil and return to the original split stance. No initial bounce or deeper dip. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: Make the starting squat shallower instead if rising produces a lurch; do not force a deep hold or fast knee lockout. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low roundhouse from a held split-squat start.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"m