  ('accelerator-low-roundhouse-through-an-empty-direction-gate', 'Low roundhouse through an empty direction gate', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-roundhouse-through-an-empty-direction-gate","name":"Low roundhouse through an empty direction gate","family":"Reactive agility output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"reactive_agility_tumbling_output","slot":"accelerator_output_reactive","cardSummary":"Directly preserve hip-led acceleration while controlling the kick direction and recovery endpoint.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Directly preserve hip-led acceleration while controlling the kick direction and recovery endpoint. The coach identifies an empty low kick line with cones placed outside the sweep and a visual height reference from outside reach. From a stationary rear-leg stance, kick through that line below hip height, keep the knee soft, recoil and recover. Nothing is struck. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a wider visual window or shorter arc instead if accuracy causes knee lockout or leaning; target accuracy alone is not a valid rep. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low roundhouse through an empty direction gate.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Directly preserve hip-led acceleration while controlling the kick direction and recovery endpoint.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls. The reactive agility tumbling output placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not shorten recovery, add fatigue reps, or continue after speed, landing, direction, or release quality declines.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequirements":{"primary_joint_actions":["rotate_pattern_control"],"primary_tissues":["full_body"],"primary_motor_control_demands":["reactive_agility_tumbling_output"],"breathing_demand":"continuous breathing without bracing or breath-holding drift","balance_demand":"moderate","coordination_demand":"moderate","impact_level":1},"coachingExecution":{"movement_description":"Directly preserve hip-led acceleration while controlling the kick direction and recovery endpoint. The coach identifies an empty low kick line with cones placed outside the sweep and a visual height reference from outside reach. From a stationary rear-leg stance, kick through that line below hip height, keep the knee soft, recoil and recover. Nothing is struck. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a wider visual window or shorter arc instead if accuracy causes knee lockout or leaning; target accuracy alone is not a valid rep. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","setup":["Prepare Bodyweight, Cleared movement area, Cones outside motion path; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Directly preserve hip-led acceleration while controlling the kick direction and recovery endpoint."],"execution_steps":["Directly preserve hip-led acceleration while controlling the kick direction and recovery endpoint.","The coach identifies an empty low kick line with cones placed outside the sweep and a visual height reference from outside reach.","From a stationary rear-leg stance, kick through that line below hip height, keep the knee soft, recoil and recover.","Nothing is struck.","Complete 1 × 2 per side/direction; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"reps","default_sets":1,"default_reps":2,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":60,"est_seconds_per_set":45,"default_rpe_min":7,"default_rpe_max":9},"scaling":{"youth_beginner":"Reduce load, range, speed, distance, impact, and decision demand. Use one coached rep at a time and stop at the first loss of control.","youth_intermediate":"Use the written pattern at a conservative dose; progress one variable only after repeated clean sessions.","teen":"Use the class prescription when readiness and technique support it; keep full recovery for explosive work and clean reps in reserve for strength.","adult_beginner":"Begin below the written load, range, or speed and increase only after the exact start and finish remain repeatable.","adult_advanced":"Use the written variation and progress one measurable constraint at a time without changing the movement identity.","older_adult":"Reduce impact, speed, range, and balance demand; add stable support and longer transitions as needed.","pregnancy_postpartum":"Use an individually cleared lower-impact, lower-load option; avoid breath holding, unstable balance, uncomfortable positions, and symptom-provoking impact."},"genderSpecificNotes":"No default gender-based load split; scale to current technique, training history, symptoms, recovery, and pregnancy/postpartum considerations.","pairsWellAfter":["Prepare & Access movement matching the exercise pattern"],"pairsWellBefore":["Full prescribed recovery before the next output exposure"],"doNotUseWhen":["The exact station, equipment, supervision, or clearance cannot be established.","Pain, dizziness, unusual breathlessness, instability, or a participant request to stop is present.","The athlete cannot preserve the named setup and finish at the planned dose."],"goodForSessions":["athletic_output"],"mediaReferences":["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BZmIA4Sseco","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GoevMondYIs","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9G5Bd_DaP24"],"mediaInternalNotes":["Three embeddable YouTube references are attached. Closest researched movement-family source: Roundhouse kick chamber, pivot, and re-chamber technique (curated YouTube family research (2026-09-14)).","The written card is authoritative for the exact Accelerator stance, direction, support, finish, dose, and safety boundary; do not infer an unshown variation from a video."],"difficultyProfile":{"technical":5,"load":3,"complexity":3,"overall":5,"recommended_age_min":6,"recommended_age_max":null,"attention_demand":"moderate","notes":"Exercise difficulty describes the task; workout readiness remains athlete-specific."},"safety":{"risk_level":1,"impact_level":1,"requires_spotting":false,"requires_coach_supervision":"recommended","readiness_checks":["Confirm the exact station, equipment, surface, clearance, and stop signal.","Confirm the athlete can demonstrate the named start and finish at a lower rehearsal intensity.","Confirm current symptoms, fatigue, and recent workload permit the prescribed exposure."],"contraindications":["Pain, acute injury concern, unsafe equipment or surface, or inability to follow the stop signal."],"common_substitutions":["Use the documented class substitution only after its equipment, dose, duration, and loading are rechecked."]},"regimen":{"can_be_daily":false,"weekly_max_frequency":3,"minimum_hours_between_hard_exposures":24,"counts_as_high_intensity":true,"counts_as_high_impact":false,"counts_as_neural":true,"counts_as_tissue_stress":false,"counts_as_conditioning":false},"phaseProfile":{"role":"primary","fit_weight":5,"freshness_required":true,"fatigue_cost":4,"fatigue_sensitivity":4,"technical_complexity":3,"impact_level":1,"intensity_ceiling":"max"},"videoDonor":"Roundhouse kick chamber, pivot, and re-chamber technique"}'::jsonb),
  ('accelerator-low-roundhouse-to-suspended-re-chamber', 'Low roundhouse to suspended re-chamber', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-roundhouse-to-suspended-re-chamber","name":"Low roundhouse to suspended re-chamber","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Directly train the rapid return and controlled arrest of the kicking leg, rather than allowing it to fall after extension.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Directly train the rapid return and controlled arrest of the kicking leg, rather than allowing it to fall after extension. From a stationary rear-leg kick stance, perform one low roundhouse. Immediately fold the knee and recover the thigh to a low chamber; hold the foot off the floor for 2 s before placing it back in stance. The athlete does not jump. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a shorter extension/low chamber instead if the foot drops or the support knee twists; hold quality matters more than range. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low roundhouse to suspended re-chamber.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully befo