  ('accelerator-low-roundhouse-with-forward-step-down-finish', 'Low roundhouse with forward step-down finish', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-roundhouse-with-forward-step-down-finish","name":"Low roundhouse with forward step-down finish","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Control residual forward/rotational momentum when the kicking leg becomes the next lead foot.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Control residual forward/rotational momentum when the kicking leg becomes the next lead foot. From a stationary rear-leg stance, execute a low controlled roundhouse and fold the knee, then place that foot into a short forward split stance instead of returning it to the original rear position. Arrest the pelvis with both feet aligned; no spinning through or second kick. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: less kick arc and a shorter step-down instead if the athlete over-rotates or lands across the support foot. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low roundhouse with forward step-down finish.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully b