hlete over-rotates or lands across the support foot. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","setup":["Prepare Bodyweight, Cleared movement area; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Control residual forward/rotational momentum when the kicking leg becomes the next lead foot."],"execution_steps":["Control residual forward/rotational momentum when the kicking leg becomes the next lead foot.","From a stationary rear-leg stance, execute a low controlled roundhouse and fold the knee, then place that foot into a short forward split stance instead of returning it to the original rear position.","Arrest the pelvis with both feet aligned; no spinning through or second kick.","A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution.","Complete 1 × 2 per side/direction; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"reps","default_sets":1,"default_reps":2,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":60,"est_seconds_per_set":45,"default_rpe_min"