  ('accelerator-low-two-foot-pogos', 'Low two-foot pogos', '{"slug":"accelerator-low-two-foot-pogos","name":"Low two-foot pogos","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Provides a small, countable two-foot elastic exposure after ankling and before the stationary movement checkpoints.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"Begin tall with knees soft and arms relaxed or held in a consistent position. Make a small two-foot hop using a quick ankle-led push. Land on both feet in the same footprint with a quiet, controlled contact. Repeat for exactly 10 contacts, then settle to a balanced stop.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Low two-foot pogos.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"ankle","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Provides a small, countable two-foot elastic exposure after ankling and before the stationary movement checkpoints.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not chase fatigue, force range, or continue through a loss of joint, trunk, landing, or balance control.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement i