  ('accelerator-med-ball-countermovement-rotational-throw-floor-target', 'Med Ball Countermovement Rotational Throw — floor target', '{"slug":"accelerator-med-ball-countermovement-rotational-throw-floor-target","name":"Med Ball Countermovement Rotational Throw — floor target","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Turn one compact preload immediately into release.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Turn one compact preload immediately into release. Stand side-on with a light ball near the rear hip; make one small wind-back then reverse into a two-hand scoop release. Feet may pivot; no entry step or repeated rocking. Hold the finish for 2 seconds. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Use instead: Reduce wind-back range if the athlete pauses, overtwists or loses direction. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Med Ball Countermovement Rotational Throw — floor target.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"phy