  ('accelerator-med-ball-shuffle-to-rotation-throw-short-floor-target-version', 'Med Ball Shuffle-to-Rotation Throw — short floor-target version', '{"slug":"accelerator-med-ball-shuffle-to-rotation-throw-short-floor-target-version","name":"Med Ball Shuffle-to-Rotation Throw — short floor-target version","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Accept lateral arrival and send the turn through the hands.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Accept lateral arrival and send the turn through the hands. Start side-on; take one short uncrossed shuffle toward the target direction, plant the lead foot and make a two-hand rotational scoop release. Stay grounded and finish within the marked bay. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Keep all entry and finish footwork inside a cleared 1-metre start bay; no hop, jump or sprint. Use instead: a single side-step into the throw instead if uncrossed shuffle placement is unreliable; same dose. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Med Ball Shuffle-to-Rotation Throw — short floor-target version.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean;