  ('accelerator-pallof-press-bilateral-athletic-stance', 'Pallof Press — Bilateral Athletic Stance', '{"slug":"accelerator-pallof-press-bilateral-athletic-stance","name":"Pallof Press — Bilateral Athletic Stance","family":"Trunk and pelvic resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"trunk_pelvis_anti_movement_control","slot":"accelerator_resilience_trunk","cardSummary":"Lightly resist trunk rotation so external force remains aligned with the forward push. With a light band pulling from one side, feet parallel and knees soft, press both hands forward, hold 2 s and return without…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Lightly resist trunk rotation so external force remains aligned with the forward push. With a light band pulling from one side, feet parallel and knees soft, press both hands forward, hold 2 s and return without turning; repeat facing the opposite pull direction. Regress/stop: Use less band tension/shorter reach; stop for twisting or breath-holding.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Pallof Press — Bilateral Athletic Stance.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"push","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bands","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Lightly resist trunk rotation so external force remains aligned with the forward push. With a light band pulling from one side, feet parallel and knees soft, press both hands forward, hold 2 s and r