  ('accelerator-partner-manual-resistance-hamstring-curl', 'Partner Manual-Resistance Hamstring Curl', '{"slug":"accelerator-partner-manual-resistance-hamstring-curl","name":"Partner Manual-Resistance Hamstring Curl","family":"Hinge and posterior-chain strength","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"hinge_posterior_chain_strength","slot":"accelerator_capacity_hinge","cardSummary":"Direct knee-flexor force supports control of the lower leg through the first running steps.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Direct knee-flexor force supports control of the lower leg through the first running steps.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Partner Manual-Resistance Hamstring Curl.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Own the position and finish every rep with two or three good reps still available.","participantStructure":"pairs","tenets":[{"key":"strength","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"resistance_calisthenics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"force_tissue_capacity","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"hinge","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Direct knee-flexor force supports control of the lower leg through the first running steps.","whyItGoesHere":"Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve. The hinge posterior chain strength placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not turn the strength prescription into a timed circuit, grind failed repetitions, or add load before the exact position is controlled.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, di