  ('accelerator-paused-split-stance-vertical-scoop-toss-no-flight', 'Paused Split-Stance Vertical Scoop Toss — no flight', '{"slug":"accelerator-paused-split-stance-vertical-scoop-toss-no-flight","name":"Paused Split-Stance Vertical Scoop Toss — no flight","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Transfer a settled lead-leg-biased force impulse into upward/slightly forward underhand release while keeping the trunk square. Both feet support the base; forefeet remain on the floor and heels may rise. Extend legs…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Transfer a settled lead-leg-biased force impulse into upward/slightly forward underhand release while keeping the trunk square. Both feet support the base; forefeet remain on the floor and heels may rise. Extend legs and carry the ball through continuously, without re-dip, twist, arm-only heave or backward lean. This changes the moving split scoop and the earlier parallel pause. Reduce load/stagger/depth if rapid leg-led release is lost. Wait for ball settlement and the coach''s clear retrieval signal; no return catch.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Paused Split-Stance Vertical Scoop Toss — no flight.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"push","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"medicine_ball","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"sh