  ('accelerator-point-cued-open-step-hip-turn', 'Point-cued open-step hip turn', '{"slug":"accelerator-point-cued-open-step-hip-turn","name":"Point-cued open-step hip turn","family":"Reactive agility output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"reactive_agility_tumbling_output","slot":"accelerator_output_reactive","cardSummary":"Select the support/turn direction before the leg-driven release.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Select the support/turn direction before the leg-driven release. Begin square and still. After the coach points left or right, take one short opening step and turn the feet/pelvis toward that line, then hold a kick stance 2 s. Cue is given before any movement; no kick or jump. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: an announced direction instead if cue errors dominate; preserve the same physical drill and record a planned version. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Point-cued open-step hip turn.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"b