  ('accelerator-prone-light-dumbbell-horizontal-arm-raise', 'Prone light-dumbbell horizontal arm raise', '{"slug":"accelerator-prone-light-dumbbell-horizontal-arm-raise","name":"Prone light-dumbbell horizontal arm raise","family":"Joint and tissue resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"slow_eccentric_isometric_joint_resilience","slot":"accelerator_resilience_tissue","cardSummary":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness. Control the posterior shoulder during the return from a released arm path. Lie chest-supported on a stable bench with light dumbbells hanging. Raise both arms outward only to a comfortable line below shoulder height, elbows soft; lower in 3 seconds without lifting the chest. Use less load/range if the neck tightens or trunk extends.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Prone light-dumbbell horizontal arm raise.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"dumbbell","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","whyItGoesHere":"Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing l