  ('accelerator-pulsing-pogo-jump-alternating-low-modestly-taller', 'Pulsing Pogo Jump — alternating low/modestly taller', '{"slug":"accelerator-pulsing-pogo-jump-alternating-low-modestly-taller","name":"Pulsing Pogo Jump — alternating low/modestly taller","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Adjust ankle impulse while keeping the body tall and the landing under the hips. Both feet leave/land together; keep knee motion small and the taller contacts clearly submaximal. Count all six landings, including the…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Adjust ankle impulse while keeping the body tall and the landing under the hips. Both feet leave/land together; keep knee motion small and the taller contacts clearly submaximal. Count all six landings, including the final stop. The sequence has three low and three modestly taller ankle flights; do not turn the latter into deep squat jumps. Reduce the amplitude difference or use uniform low pogos for loud contacts, collapse, drift or rhythm loss.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Pulsing Pogo Jump — alternating low/modestly taller.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"ankle","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Adjust ankle impulse while keeping the body tall and th