  ('accelerator-push-up-controlled-full-repetition', 'Push-Up — controlled full repetition', '{"slug":"accelerator-push-up-controlled-full-repetition","name":"Push-Up — controlled full repetition","family":"Upper-body push strength","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"upper_body_push_strength","slot":"accelerator_capacity_push","cardSummary":"Strengthen the press with shoulder blades free to move and the trunk held as one unit, complementing the floor-supported press. Use 2 seconds down, a decisive ascent and 1 second at the top; finish by pushing the floor away without adding a separate scapular cycle. Choose hand elevation or band resistance so 8 reps leave 2–3 in reserve. No hand flight.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Keep the working load at 2–3 technical reps/cycles in reserve. Strengthen the press with shoulder blades free to move and the trunk held as one unit, complementing the floor-supported press. Use 2 seconds down, a decisive ascent and 1 second at the top; finish by pushing the floor away without adding a separate scapular cycle. Choose hand elevation or band resistance so 8 reps leave 2–3 in reserve. No hand flight. Use instead: higher stable hand support or appropriate resistance to retain the same controlled reps and technical reserve. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Push-Up — controlled full repetition.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Own the position and finish every rep with two or three good reps still available.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"strength","weight":5}],