 resistance to retain the same controlled reps and technical reserve. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","setup":["Prepare Bodyweight; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Keep the working load at 2–3 technical reps/cycles in reserve."],"execution_steps":["Keep the working load at 2–3 technical reps/cycles in reserve.","Strengthen the press with shoulder blades free to move and the trunk held as one unit, complementing the floor-supported press.","Use 2 seconds down, a decisive ascent and 1 second at the top; finish by pushing the floor away without adding a separate scapular cycle.","Choose hand elevation or band resistance so 8 reps leave 2–3 in reserve.","Complete 1 × 8; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Control the full usable range and stop before compensation."],"athlete_cues":["Own the position from start to finish.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Adding load, range, or speed after position quality changes.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"reps","default_sets":1,"default_reps":8,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":120,"est_seconds_per_set":60,"default_rpe_min":6,"default_rpe_max":8},"scaling":{"youth_beginner":"Reduce load, range, speed, distance, impact, and decision demand. Use one coached rep at a time and stop at the first loss of control.","youth_intermediate":"Us