  ('accelerator-repeated-vertical-jump-two-consecutive-jumps-final-stick', 'Repeated Vertical Jump — two consecutive jumps, final stick', '{"slug":"accelerator-repeated-vertical-jump-two-consecutive-jumps-final-stick","name":"Repeated Vertical Jump — two consecutive jumps, final stick","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Accept the first vertical receiver and reuse it for another upward leg push. Start with parallel feet and a comfortable knee/hip dip; jump twice without a deliberate pause between them, then hold the final bilateral…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Accept the first vertical receiver and reuse it for another upward leg push. Start with parallel feet and a comfortable knee/hip dip; jump twice without a deliberate pause between them, then hold the final bilateral landing 2 s. Keep the knees tracking and the torso controlled. Do not take the second jump if the first receiver collapses, twists or needs a deep recovery squat.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Repeated Vertical Jump — two consecutive jumps, final stick.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Accept the first vertical receiver and reuse it for another upward leg push. Start w