  ('accelerator-retreat-step-low-roundhouse-counter', 'Retreat-step low roundhouse counter', '{"slug":"accelerator-retreat-step-low-roundhouse-counter","name":"Retreat-step low roundhouse counter","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Directly change backward bodyweight travel into a controlled rotational counter action.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Directly change backward bodyweight travel into a controlled rotational counter action. Make one short retreat step onto the support leg, arrest the backward drift, turn that support foot with the pelvis and execute a low opposite-leg roundhouse. Recoil into a stable stance within the 2 m segment. No opponent or pad. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a smaller/slower retreat or a brief settled plant instead if the athlete continues drifting; do not reach with the kick to compensate. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Retreat-step low roundhouse counter.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets