  ('accelerator-rotational-shadow-uppercut', 'Rotational shadow uppercut', '{"slug":"accelerator-rotational-shadow-uppercut","name":"Rotational shadow uppercut","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Knee drive → rising hand path: Keep the hovering-leg drive and uppercut connected to a tall trunk without substituting a back arch for limb acceleration.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Knee drive → rising hand path: Keep the hovering-leg drive and uppercut connected to a tall trunk without substituting a back arch for limb acceleration. Link a compact turn to an upward bent-arm hand path. No target or implement. With elbow bent, move the fist from lower-rib height toward chin height as the rear foot/hip turns; stop before the shoulder shrugs. No deep squat or overhead punch. Shorten the upward path if the low back extends or the arm separates from the turn. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Rotational shadow uppercut.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Knee drive → rising hand path: Keep the hovering-leg drive and uppercut connected to a tall trunk without substituting a back arch for limb acceleration.","