  ('accelerator-seated-sprint-start-first-two-steps', 'Seated Sprint Start — first two steps', '{"slug":"accelerator-seated-sprint-start-first-two-steps","name":"Seated Sprint Start — first two steps","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Main task: transfer support from the seat to the feet and initiate forward travel without backward rocking. Sit at the front of a stable fitted bench/box, both feet flat near hip width, knees comfortably bent and trunk…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main task: transfer support from the seat to the feet and initiate forward travel without backward rocking. Sit at the front of a stable fitted bench/box, both feet flat near hip width, knees comfortably bent and trunk slightly inclined forward. Settle for 2 s, then push up/forward through the legs and take the selected first step; arms assist naturally but hands do not push the seat. First pair uses controlled fast intent to establish stopping; second uses the fastest clean intent that preserves it. No jump off the seat.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Seated Sprint Start — first two steps.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"locomote","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bench","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Main task: transfer support from the seat to th