  ('accelerator-short-crossover-to-band-backhand-speed-sweep', 'Short crossover-to-band backhand speed sweep', '{"slug":"accelerator-short-crossover-to-band-backhand-speed-sweep","name":"Short crossover-to-band backhand speed sweep","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Brake the entry while accelerating and stopping a retained transverse load.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Brake the entry while accelerating and stopping a retained transverse load. With a light side-anchored band, take a small step behind and replant the lead foot. After a secure plant, turn and sweep both hands across the chest-height arc, then return slowly and reset feet. Verify the stated band anchor and tension; retain the band throughout, with no release or uncontrolled recoil. Keep all entry and finish footwork inside a cleared 1-metre start bay; no hop, jump or sprint. Use instead: the stationary sweep instead if feet or band line cross unsafely. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Short crossover-to-band backhand speed sweep.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neura