  ('accelerator-short-drop-step-lead-leg-roundhouse', 'Short drop-step lead-leg roundhouse', '{"slug":"accelerator-short-drop-step-lead-leg-roundhouse","name":"Short drop-step lead-leg roundhouse","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Use a compact rear-hip load to free the lead leg while retaining the planned kick line.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Use a compact rear-hip load to free the lead leg while retaining the planned kick line. The kicking leg begins in front. Take one small rear-foot drop step to load the support hip, turn that foot freely and deliver a low lead-leg roundhouse without another gather. Recoil into a comfortable split stance; stay within 2 m. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a shallower drop step instead if the lead leg drags or the support knee twists; do not add speed and step length together. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Short drop-step lead-leg roundhouse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosivene