  ('accelerator-single-arm-diagonal-battle-rope-downstroke', 'Single-arm diagonal battle-rope downstroke', '{"slug":"accelerator-single-arm-diagonal-battle-rope-downstroke","name":"Single-arm diagonal battle-rope downstroke","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Called landing → diagonal stop: Choose the jump direction before takeoff and own the landing; separately stop a single diagonal rope pulse from a planned stance.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Called landing → diagonal stop: Choose the jump direction before takeoff and own the landing; separately stop a single diagonal rope pulse from a planned stance. Control a unilateral downward rotational impulse. With one manageable rope end near upper-chest height, pivot and drive the working hand toward the opposite front pocket. Keep a soft elbow, long trunk and short path; settle completely before resetting. Use an unloaded diagonal hand drive instead if rope load prevents clean control. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Single-arm diagonal battle-rope downstroke.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"battle_rope","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Called landing → diagonal stop: Choose the jump direction bef