  ('accelerator-single-arm-dumbbell-floor-press', 'Single-arm Dumbbell Floor Press', '{"slug":"accelerator-single-arm-dumbbell-floor-press","name":"Single-arm Dumbbell Floor Press","family":"Upper-body push strength","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"upper_body_push_strength","slot":"accelerator_capacity_push","cardSummary":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern. Load terminal horizontal pressing force for source E4 after rotation has brought the arm forward. Lie supine, feet comfortably planted, one dumbbell above the chest; lower in 3 seconds until the upper arm gently meets the floor, pause briefly and press. Keep ribs/pelvis level; no bridge or torso roll. Rest 90 seconds between sides. This isolates the release-side press more than source P2''s integrated upward arc; one working set limits overlap. Use less load if the elbow lands hard or the trunk rolls.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Single-arm Dumbbell Floor Press.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Own the position and finish every rep with two or three good reps still available.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"strength","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"resistance_calisthenics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"force_tissue_capacity","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"push","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"dumbbell","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern.","whyItGoe