  ('accelerator-single-arm-rotational-battle-rope-uppercut-pulse', 'Single-arm rotational battle-rope uppercut pulse', '{"slug":"accelerator-single-arm-rotational-battle-rope-uppercut-pulse","name":"Single-arm rotational battle-rope uppercut pulse","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Rear-leg push → rising hand force: Create a short grounded forward push, then connect a settled foot/hip turn to the rising single-arm rope pulse.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Rear-leg push → rising hand force: Create a short grounded forward push, then connect a settled foot/hip turn to the rising single-arm rope pulse. Express the upward diagonal through one arm. Hold one manageable rope end near the working hip. Pivot and drive the bent arm toward opposite upper-chest height in one compact pulse; stop and settle completely before reset. Keep the other end clear. Use the unloaded uppercut replacement if rope load prevents a quick clean pulse. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Single-arm rotational battle-rope uppercut pulse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"battle_rope","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Rear-leg push → rising hand force: Create a short g