  ('accelerator-single-arm-rotational-medicine-ball-hook-throw', 'Single-arm rotational medicine-ball hook throw', '{"slug":"accelerator-single-arm-rotational-medicine-ball-hook-throw","name":"Single-arm rotational medicine-ball hook throw","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Couple a bent-arm transverse release to the trunk turn.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Couple a bent-arm transverse release to the trunk turn. Hold a securely grippable light ball at the rear side of the chest, elbow bent near 90 degrees. Pivot and turn while sweeping the bent forearm through a short forward/transverse arc into the low target. Avoid a long backswing or forceful elbow lock. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Use instead: the two-hand backhand throw instead if one-hand grip or shoulder position is insecure. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Single-arm rotational medicine-ball hook throw.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometr