  ('accelerator-single-leg-takeoff-to-two-foot-box-landing', 'Single-leg Takeoff to Two-foot Box Landing', '{"slug":"accelerator-single-leg-takeoff-to-two-foot-box-landing","name":"Single-leg Takeoff to Two-foot Box Landing","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Main task: direct one leg''s dip-to-drive force upward. Start stationary on one foot, free foot clear; no approach or repeated hop. Swing the arms, extend the stance leg and land on a low stable box with both whole feet.…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main task: direct one leg''s dip-to-drive force upward. Start stationary on one foot, free foot clear; no approach or repeated hop. Swing the arms, extend the stance leg and land on a low stable box with both whole feet. Hold 2 s, stand and step down. Choose a small gap and easily controlled target, not a height challenge. Lower box/intent or use the floor replacement for knee collapse, pelvic rotation, deep tuck or edge contact.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Single-leg Takeoff to Two-foot Box Landing.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"ankle","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Main task: direct one leg''s dip-to-drive force upward. Start stationary on one foot, free foot clear; no appro