  ('accelerator-single-shuffle-low-roundhouse', 'Single-shuffle low roundhouse', '{"slug":"accelerator-single-shuffle-low-roundhouse","name":"Single-shuffle low roundhouse","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Directly convert arriving lateral mass into support-foot/pelvic rotation.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Directly convert arriving lateral mass into support-foot/pelvic rotation. From a kick stance, make one short lateral shuffle toward the support side, settle that foot without an extra stutter and launch the opposite low roundhouse. Recoil and recover the stance. Entry and finish stay within 2 m; no target or continuous shuffling. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a shorter/slower single shuffle instead if the plant overstrides or the knee cannot turn freely; maintain a brisk controlled hip action. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Single-shuffle low roundhouse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","we