  ('accelerator-small-single-leg-turn-hop-to-same-leg-stick', 'Small single-leg turn hop to same-leg stick', '{"slug":"accelerator-small-single-leg-turn-hop-to-same-leg-stick","name":"Small single-leg turn hop to same-leg stick","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Single-leg orientation → constrained handoff: Control the small same-leg turning hop and then the kneeling supplied push with a stable support position.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Single-leg orientation → constrained handoff: Control the small same-leg turning hop and then the kneeling supplied push with a stable support position. Qualify control of rotational force on the leg that must remain the kick support. Only use the single-leg version after a controlled small unturned hop is known. Otherwise use instead a single-leg takeoff to a two-foot turning catch, same four flights; record four bilateral instead of unilateral landings.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Small single-leg turn hop to same-leg stick.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Single-leg orientation → constrained handoff: Control the small same-leg turning hop and then the kneeling supplied push with a stable supp