  ('accelerator-split-squat-stationary-dumbbells', 'Split Squat — stationary, dumbbells', '{"slug":"accelerator-split-squat-stationary-dumbbells","name":"Split Squat — stationary, dumbbells","family":"Squat and knee-dominant strength","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"squat_knee_dominant_strength","slot":"accelerator_capacity_squat","cardSummary":"Primary strength investment: challenge each lead leg''s force in a stable split base, supporting each leg''s contribution to an organized bilateral rebound. Keep rear forefoot grounded, pelvis square and the whole front…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Primary strength investment: challenge each lead leg''s force in a stable split base, supporting each leg''s contribution to an organized bilateral rebound. Keep rear forefoot grounded, pelvis square and the whole front foot loaded; use secure light support if balance limits force. Reduce load/range for knee/pelvis loss or a grind. The second round is performed only while current technique, effort and recovery remain suitable; stop/reduce rather than make up missed reps elsewhere.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Split Squat — stationary, dumbbells.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Own the position and finish every rep with two or three good reps still available.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"strength","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"resistance_calisthenics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"force_tissue_capacity","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"squat","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"dumbbell","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Primary strength investment: challenge each lead leg''s force i