  ('accelerator-split-stance-anti-rotation-row-light-band', 'Split-Stance Anti-Rotation Row — light band', '{"slug":"accelerator-split-stance-anti-rotation-row-light-band","name":"Split-Stance Anti-Rotation Row — light band","family":"Joint and tissue resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"slow_eccentric_isometric_joint_resilience","slot":"accelerator_resilience_tissue","cardSummary":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness. Control the trunk against a moving arm force while the planted base stays fixed. Band ahead and slightly to the working side. In split stance, row lightly toward lower ribs without rotating the trunk or shifting feet; return in 3 seconds and breathe. Reduce tension/reach if the pelvis turns or balance becomes the limiting task.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Split-Stance Anti-Rotation Row — light band.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bands","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","whyItGoesHere":"Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing lat