  ('accelerator-split-stance-auditory-sprint-start-first-two-steps', 'Split-Stance Auditory Sprint Start — first two steps', '{"slug":"accelerator-split-stance-auditory-sprint-start-first-two-steps","name":"Split-Stance Auditory Sprint Start — first two steps","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Main task: preserve a useful staggered push while waiting for an external start signal. Use a comfortable two-point stagger and forward whole-body inclination, hands free. After the athlete settles, the coach waits an…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main task: preserve a useful staggered push while waiting for an external start signal. Use a comfortable two-point stagger and forward whole-body inclination, hands free. After the athlete settles, the coach waits an unannounced 2–4 s, then says one clear, non-startling “go” from a verified position outside the lane. Push straight forward with natural opposing arms; no rocking, backward step or guessed launch. First pair is controlled-fast to establish stopping; faster intent in the second requires control. Do not force an upright transition in two steps.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Split-Stance Auditory Sprint Start — first two steps.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"locomote","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":