  ('accelerator-split-stance-band-resisted-knee-drive-light-band', 'Split-Stance Band-Resisted Knee Drive — light band', '{"slug":"accelerator-split-stance-band-resisted-knee-drive-light-band","name":"Split-Stance Band-Resisted Knee Drive — light band","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Support the moving limb: Use the knee drive to own the stance leg, then reduce leg propulsion in the kneeling throw and keep the pelvis and trunk organized.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Support the moving limb: Use the knee drive to own the stance leg, then reduce leg propulsion in the kneeling throw and keep the pelvis and trunk organized. Give the free thigh a small resisted acceleration demand, isolating chamber initiation from E3''s full kick. Keep the pelvis quiet and support foot secure. Reduce band tension for slow movement, toe snagging or trunk lean. If a suitable secure loop is unavailable, use instead an unresisted split-stance knee drive at the same dose; record the resistance change.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Split-Stance Band-Resisted Knee Drive — light band.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bands","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support the moving limb: Use the knee drive to 