  ('accelerator-split-stance-broad-jump-fixed-lead-two-foot-reception', 'Split-Stance Broad Jump — fixed lead, two-foot reception', '{"slug":"accelerator-split-stance-broad-jump-fixed-lead-two-foot-reception","name":"Split-Stance Broad Jump — fixed lead, two-foot reception","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Main asymmetric leg contribution to a forward push while retaining a bilateral landing. Start in a modest split stance, front whole foot loaded and rear foot assisting. Use one small dip and project a short distance;…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main asymmetric leg contribution to a forward push while retaining a bilateral landing. Start in a modest split stance, front whole foot loaded and rear foot assisting. Use one small dip and project a short distance; land with feet parallel and hold 2 s. Repeat with the other lead leg; this is not a single-leg takeoff. Recovery: 90 s between complete set rounds; complete one leg''s bout, rest 60 s, then the other leg; 8 total reps; 10 s between individual reps; 90 s before the next exercise/section Use instead: a shorter split-stance jump, or the Week 1 parallel broad jump if asymmetry loses the forward line; record the changed start. This replaces remaining work in this slot; follow an explicit replacement dose if stated, otherwise keep the remaining dose/rest. Log changed events or laterality.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Split-Stance Broad Jump — fixed lead, two-foot reception.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","p