p if asymmetry loses the forward line; record the changed start. This replaces remaining work in this slot; follow an explicit replacement dose if stated, otherwise keep the remaining dose/rest. Log changed events or laterality.","setup":["Prepare Bodyweight; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Main asymmetric leg contribution to a forward push while retaining a bilateral landing."],"execution_steps":["Main asymmetric leg contribution to a forward push while retaining a bilateral landing.","Start in a modest split stance, front whole foot loaded and rear foot assisting.","Use one small dip and project a short distance; land with feet parallel and hold 2 s.","Repeat with the other lead leg; this is not a single-leg takeoff.","Complete 2 × 2 per leg; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"reps","default_sets":2,"default_reps":2,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":90,"est_seconds_per_set":45,"default_rpe_min":7,"default_rpe_max":9},"scaling":{"youth_beginner":"Reduce load, range, speed, distance, impact, and decision demand. Use one coached rep at a time and stop at the first loss of control.","youth_intermediate":"Use the written pattern at a conservative dose; progress on