  ('accelerator-split-stance-explosive-hip-pivot', 'Split-stance explosive hip pivot', '{"slug":"accelerator-split-stance-explosive-hip-pivot","name":"Split-stance explosive hip pivot","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Repeat the small grounded hip-pivot reference to organize initiation and a still finish. It follows the linear force tasks in this combined class; use current quality unless actual earlier preparation and preceding workload also match.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Repeat the small grounded hip-pivot reference to organize initiation and a still finish. It follows the linear force tasks in this combined class; use current quality unless actual earlier preparation and preceding workload also match. Use a short split stance and a comfortable grounded hip-and-foot turn of about 45 degrees or less. Both forefeet stay down as the heels may release. Turn feet and pelvis together and finish still for 2 seconds. Mirror the stance for the other side; no kick or jump. Let the support foot or both feet turn freely with the pelvis; never force rotation through a trapped knee. Remain grounded. Use instead: Reduce the turn size or stop if foot release and knee alignment cannot be controlled. Record changed stance or angle as a changed comparison condition. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Split-stance explosive hip pivot.” Preserve its de