  ('accelerator-split-stance-pallof-press-light-band', 'Split-Stance Pallof Press — light band', '{"slug":"accelerator-split-stance-pallof-press-light-band","name":"Split-Stance Pallof Press — light band","family":"Trunk and pelvic resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"trunk_pelvis_anti_movement_control","slot":"accelerator_resilience_trunk","cardSummary":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness. Maintain the stacked finish against an external turning pull. Band at sternum height to the side; mirror the anchor-facing side and lead foot. Press forward without the ribs or pelvis turning toward the anchor, breathe during the hold, return in 2 seconds. Use a shorter reach or lighter band instead if the torso drifts.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Split-Stance Pallof Press — light band.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"push","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bands","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","whyItGoesHere":"Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work. The trunk pelvis anti movement con