  ('accelerator-sprinter-step-up-jump-two-foot-floor-landing', 'Sprinter Step-Up Jump — Two-foot Floor Landing', '{"slug":"accelerator-sprinter-step-up-jump-two-foot-floor-landing","name":"Sprinter Step-Up Jump — Two-foot Floor Landing","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Drive through a forward supported stance leg while coordinating the free knee. Start with one entire foot on a very low stable step, drive up/forward from that leg and land on both feet on the clear floor; hold 2 s and…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Drive through a forward supported stance leg while coordinating the free knee. Start with one entire foot on a very low stable step, drive up/forward from that leg and land on both feet on the clear floor; hold 2 s and walk to reset. Regress/stop: Use a lower step and smaller flight; stop if the rear foot pushes off or the floor landing becomes a drop the athlete cannot control. Entry: Suitable low step and familiar jump-off/floor landing.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Sprinter Step-Up Jump — Two-foot Floor Landing.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"ankle","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Drive through a forward supported stance leg while coordinating the free knee. Start with one e