d intended through the nearer leg, while both feet assist.","Use a fitted stable seat and a small fore/aft offset with both feet flat, arms crossed comfortably.","Arrange torso over the nearer foot before the seated settle, stand briskly without rocking or pushing hands on the seat, then return under control.","Keep pelvis level; no jump or claimed force-sharing percentage.","Complete 1 × 2 per leg = 4 rises: the named working foot is the foot nearer the seat; the assisting foot is slightly farther forward. About 1 s rise, 1 s tall hold, 3 s lowering, 2 s seated settle. 20 s after seated reset between same-leg reps; 60 s between foot arrangements; 90 s before Section 3.; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"reps","default_sets":1,"default_reps":2,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":60,"est_seconds_per_set":45,"default_rpe_min":7,"default_rpe_max":9},"scaling":{"youth_beginner":"Reduce load, range, speed, distance, impact, and decision demand. Use one coached rep at a time and stop at the first loss of control.","youth_intermediate":"Use the written pattern at a conservative dose; progress one variable only after repeated clean sessions.","teen":"Use the class prescription when readiness and technique suppor