  ('accelerator-standing-cable-or-band-hip-flexion', 'Standing Cable or Band Hip Flexion', '{"slug":"accelerator-standing-cable-or-band-hip-flexion","name":"Standing Cable or Band Hip Flexion","family":"Accessory and tissue capacity","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"tissue_capacity_isometric_eccentric_accessory","slot":"accelerator_capacity_accessory","cardSummary":"Challenge active chamber lifting and controlled lowering so the free leg can accelerate and recover while the other leg supplies the rotational base.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Keep the working load at 2–3 technical reps/cycles in reserve. Challenge active chamber lifting and controlled lowering so the free leg can accelerate and recover while the other leg supplies the rotational base. Stand upright with a secure band loop at the forefeet, the support foot anchoring its end and optional light fingertip contact on a stable support. Raise the bent knee to a comfortable low chamber with the pelvis quiet, then lower without swinging. Use about 1 second lifting, 2 seconds lowering and 1 second resetting. Do not use momentum, a hop or an unsecured loop. Use instead: Reduce tension or chamber height for pelvic tipping or loss of foot security. If the loop cannot be secured, use self-resisted seated bent-knee hip flexion with the hands resisting the distal thigh instead; record the changed, less reproducible resistance. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Standing Cable or Band Hip Flexion.” Prese