  ('accelerator-standing-hip-airplane-kick-prep-hand-supported-small-range-strengthening-execution', 'Standing Hip Airplane Kick Prep — hand-supported, small-range strengthening execution', '{"slug":"accelerator-standing-hip-airplane-kick-prep-hand-supported-small-range-strengthening-execution","name":"Standing Hip Airplane Kick Prep — hand-supported, small-range strengthening execution","family":"Single-leg and lower-limb resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"single_leg_balance_foot_ankle_hip_control","slot":"accelerator_resilience_single_leg","cardSummary":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness. Apply low-load eccentric/concentric control around the support hip, limiting pelvic spill during the kick. Hand support removes balance as the limiting task. Shrink the arc or use light trailing-toe support instead if knee alignment or foot pressure changes; no forced end-range rotation.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Standing Hip Airplane Kick Prep — hand-supported, small-range strengthening execution.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bench","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"wrist","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support the shared rotational base wit