  ('accelerator-standing-low-roundhouse-shadow-kick', 'Standing low roundhouse shadow kick', '{"slug":"accelerator-standing-low-roundhouse-shadow-kick","name":"Standing low roundhouse shadow kick","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Revisit the low kick execution and dose used in combined Class 2. Preceding exercises differ, so use current movement quality unless actual equipment, preparation, order and recovery are also documented as matching.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Revisit the low kick execution and dose used in combined Class 2. Preceding exercises differ, so use current movement quality unless actual equipment, preparation, order and recovery are also documented as matching. Use a short fighting stance with the kicking leg rear and a low kick line. Turn the support foot with the pelvis, accelerate the free thigh, extend only through a controlled partial arc, actively recoil and return to the same stance with a 2-second hold. Keep the foot below hip height and the terminal knee soft. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a shorter low arc and less knee extension if control or recoil is insufficient; record changed execution instead of claiming a matched comparison. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage