  ('accelerator-standing-rotational-band-row', 'Standing rotational band row', '{"slug":"accelerator-standing-rotational-band-row","name":"Standing rotational band row","family":"Pull, hang, and grip strength","primaryPhaseKey":"capacity","subrole":"pull_hang_grip_strength","slot":"accelerator_capacity_pull","cardSummary":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator capacity block with the listed dose and recovery. Build force capacity with controlled repetitions, appropriate loading, and clean reps held in reserve.","description":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern. Load the pulling side of the turn and control the return into the next preload. Band anchored in front at lower-chest height, opposite foot forward; reach without rounding, then turn feet/hips/trunk modestly as the elbow draws toward the same-side lower ribs. Return in 3 seconds under band tension. This is a single rotational row, not a row-plus-twist combination. Rest 90 seconds between sides. Reduce tension if the shoulder hikes or the athlete yanks from the low back.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Standing rotational band row.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Own the position and finish every rep with two or three good reps still available.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"strength","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"resistance_calisthenics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"force_tissue_capacity","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bands","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"shoulder","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support today’s leg-to-trunk-to-hand force transfer with this challenging strength pattern.","whyItGoesHere":"Build force capacity with controlled