  ('accelerator-standing-single-leg-cycle-and-strike', 'Standing Single-Leg Cycle and Strike', '{"slug":"accelerator-standing-single-leg-cycle-and-strike","name":"Standing Single-Leg Cycle and Strike","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Rehearse returning the free foot beneath the pelvis while the other leg provides stable support. Keep the support foot planted. Recover the moving heel beneath the hip, bring the thigh forward through a comfortable…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Rehearse returning the free foot beneath the pelvis while the other leg provides stable support. Keep the support foot planted. Recover the moving heel beneath the hip, bring the thigh forward through a comfortable range, let the lower leg unfold without kicking, then place the foot quickly beside the support foot. No running travel or hopping on the support leg. Reduce cycle height/range for leaning, a long backswing or an ahead-of-body strike. A rep is one complete recovery-and-strike cycle.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Standing Single-Leg Cycle and Strike.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"none","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Rehearse returning the free foot beneath the pelvis while the other leg prov