  ('accelerator-standing-split-start-acceleration-2-m-full-stop', 'Standing Split-Start Acceleration — 2 m, full stop', '{"slug":"accelerator-standing-split-start-acceleration-2-m-full-stop","name":"Standing Split-Start Acceleration — 2 m, full stop","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Apply a lead-leg push to the first running steps and then regain control. Begin stationary in a comfortable split stance; push forward and accelerate for only 2 m, then decelerate within the final inspected 7 m after…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Apply a lead-leg push to the first running steps and then regain control. Begin stationary in a comfortable split stance; push forward and accelerate for only 2 m, then decelerate within the final inspected 7 m after reserving 1 m for the start stance. One attempt with each lead leg. No jump start, fall or backward rock; use submaximal effort if needed to stop comfortably. Recovery: complete one leg''s bout, rest 90 s, then the other leg; 2 total reps; 90 s before the next exercise/section Use instead: two fast grounded supported split-squat rises total, one per lead leg, when the running/stopping envelope is unsuitable; record zero sprint metres. This replaces remaining work in this slot; follow an explicit replacement dose if stated, otherwise keep the remaining dose/rest. Log changed events or laterality.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Standing Split-Start Acceleration — 2 m, full stop.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure"