  ('accelerator-stationary-single-leg-high-knee-run', 'Stationary Single-Leg High-Knee Run', '{"slug":"accelerator-stationary-single-leg-high-knee-run","name":"Stationary Single-Leg High-Knee Run","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Main task: repeatedly recover one thigh while the other leg uses a low, compact running step. Begin supported on the opposite leg with target thigh comfortably raised. Exchange onto the target foot, then onto the…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main task: repeatedly recover one thigh while the other leg uses a low, compact running step. Begin supported on the opposite leg with target thigh comfortably raised. Exchange onto the target foot, then onto the opposite foot as the target heel folds beneath the hip and its thigh rises again. Repeat this asymmetric rhythm without a full cycle on the low-step leg. Use small flight, natural arms and nearby foot contacts; do not hop twice on one foot. Finish the third cycle under control. Lower knee height/speed for long backswing, drift, reaching or backward lean.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Stationary Single-Leg High-Knee Run.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"locomote","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Main task: repeated