  ('accelerator-stationary-single-leg-hop-step-jump', 'Stationary Single-leg Hop–Step–Jump', '{"slug":"accelerator-stationary-single-leg-hop-step-jump","name":"Stationary Single-leg Hop–Step–Jump","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Integrate same-leg reuse, opposite-leg transfer and a bilateral final reception into one defined horizontal foot sequence. From one foot, hop to the same foot, step-bound to the opposite foot, then jump from that foot…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Integrate same-leg reuse, opposite-leg transfer and a bilateral final reception into one defined horizontal foot sequence. From one foot, hop to the same foot, step-bound to the opposite foot, then jump from that foot to both feet; hold the final landing. Start the other set on the opposite leg. Regress/stop: Shorten each segment and slow entry intent while keeping the sequence; stop for a collapsing intermediate contact or incorrect foot order.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Stationary Single-leg Hop–Step–Jump.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Integrate same-leg reuse, opposite-leg transfer and a bilateral final reception into one defined horizontal foot sequence. From one foot, hop to the same foot, step-bound to the opposite foot, then jump from that foot…","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls. The elastic stiffness plyometric rudiments placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not shorten recovery, add fatigue reps, or continue after speed, landing, direction, or release quality declines.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequirements":{"primary_joint_actions":["jump_pattern_control"],"primary_tissues":["hip"],"primary_motor_control_demands":["elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments"],"breathing_demand":"continuous breathing without bracing or breath-holding drift","balance_demand":"moderate-to-high","coordination_demand":"moderate","impact_level":3},"coachingExecution":{"movement_description":"Integrate same-leg reuse, opposite-leg transfer and a bilateral final reception into one defined horizontal foot sequence. From one foot, hop to the same foot, step-bound to the opposite foot, then jump from that foot to both feet; hold the final landing. Start the other set on the opposite leg. Regress/stop: Shorten each segment and slow entry intent while keeping the sequence; stop for a collapsing intermediate contact or incorrect foot order.","setup":["Prepare Box / step; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Integrate same-leg reuse, opposite-leg transfer and a bilateral final reception into one defined horizontal foot sequence."],"execution_steps":["Integrate same-leg reuse, opposite-leg transfer and a bilateral final reception into one defined horizontal foot sequence.","From one foot, hop to the same foot, step-bound to the opposite foot, then jump from that foot to both feet; hold the final landing.","Start the other set on the opposite le