he opposite leg uses a low running step.","Use small flight and natural arms; no kick, backward claw or literal obstacle to clear.","Lower the release range/cadence for reaching, leaning or extra hops.","Complete 1 × 2 cycles per target leg, bodyweight; 75 s between target legs. One target-foot contact + one low opposite-foot contact = one cycle: 8 total running contacts, 4/foot.; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"contacts","default_sets":1,"default_reps":2,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":90,"est_seconds_per_set":45,"default_rpe_min":7,"default_rpe_max":9},"scaling":{"youth_beginner":"Reduce load, range, speed, distance, impact, and decision demand. Use one coached rep at a time and stop at the first loss of control.","youth_intermediate":"Use the written pattern at a conservative dose; progress one variable only after repeated clean sessions.","teen":"Use the class prescription when readiness and technique support it; keep full recovery for explosive work and clean reps in reserve for strength.","adult_beginner":"Begin below the written load, range, or speed and increase only after the exact start and finish remain repeatable.","adult_advanced":"Use the written variation and progress one measurable 