  ('accelerator-step-behind-gathered-low-roundhouse', 'Step-behind gathered low roundhouse', '{"slug":"accelerator-step-behind-gathered-low-roundhouse","name":"Step-behind gathered low roundhouse","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Gathered entry → supplied lateral entry: Uncross and settle the step-behind kick entry, then organize handoff, lateral step and backhand release without rushing the base.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Gathered entry → supplied lateral entry: Uncross and settle the step-behind kick entry, then organize handoff, lateral step and backhand release without rushing the base. Sample how a compact step-behind load can feed the known hip-led kick. Use a very small non-crossing gather instead if foot clearance is doubtful; log that replacement. One attempt per leg is a probe, not a mastery claim.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Step-behind gathered low roundhouse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Gathered entry → supplied lateral entry: Uncross and settle the step-behind kick entry, then organize handoff, lateral step and backhand release without rushing the base.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls. The jump throw explosive power placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not shorten recovery, add fatigue reps, or continue after speed, landing, direction, or release quality declines.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequirements":{"primary_joint_actions":["rotate_pattern_control"],"primary_tissues":["full_body"],"primary_motor_control_demands":["jump_throw_explosive_power"],"breathing_demand":"continuous breathing without bracing or breath-holding drift","balance_demand":"moderate","coordination_demand":"moderate","impact_level":1},"coachingExecution":{"movement_description":"Gathered entry → supplied lateral entry: Uncross and settle the step-behind kick entry, then organize handoff, lateral step and backhand release without rushing the base. Sample how a compact step-behind load can feed the known hip-led kick. Use a very small non-crossing gather instead if foot clearance is doubtful; log that replacement. One attempt per leg is a probe, not a mastery claim.","setup":["Prepare Marked space; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Gathered entry → supplied lateral entry: Uncross and settle the step-behind kick entry, then organize handoff, lateral step and backhand release without rushing the base."],"execution_steps":["Gathered entry → supplied lateral entry: Uncross and settle the step-behind kick entry, then organize handoff, lateral step and backhand release without rushing the base.","Sample how a compact step-behind load can feed the known hip-led kick.","Use a very small non-crossing gather instead if foot clearance is doubtful; log that replacement.","One attempt per leg is a probe, not a mastery claim.","Complete 1 × 1 per kicking leg = 2 attempts. Use one short step-behind gat