  ('accelerator-step-down-to-step-up-quick-grounded-reversal', 'Step-Down to Step-Up — quick grounded reversal', '{"slug":"accelerator-step-down-to-step-up-quick-grounded-reversal","name":"Step-Down to Step-Up — quick grounded reversal","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Accept a small controlled lowering then push through the lead foot without flight. Stand with both feet on a low inspected step. Keep the lead foot planted, lower the other heel to a light floor touch in 2 s, then drive…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Accept a small controlled lowering then push through the lead foot without flight. Stand with both feet on a low inspected step. Keep the lead foot planted, lower the other heel to a light floor touch in 2 s, then drive back up quickly until both feet join. Two complete down-and-up reps per lead leg. Do not bounce from the floor foot. Recovery: complete one leg''s bout, rest 45 s, then the other leg; 4 total reps; 10 s between individual reps; 90 s before the next exercise/section Use instead: a shallow supported single-leg squat lower-and-rise at the same per-leg dose if the step height or path is unsuitable. This replaces remaining work in this slot; follow an explicit replacement dose if stated, otherwise keep the remaining dose/rest. Log changed events or laterality.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Step-Down to Step-Up — quick grounded reversal.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explo