  ('accelerator-supported-calf-pop-to-low-knee-chamber', 'Supported calf-pop to low knee chamber', '{"slug":"accelerator-supported-calf-pop-to-low-knee-chamber","name":"Supported calf-pop to low knee chamber","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a free foot/hip turn to produce one modest upward rope pulse.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a free foot/hip turn to produce one modest upward rope pulse. Coordinate the ankle-led heel release with unloading the free leg, without another landing. Use a smaller heel rise/chamber instead if the ankle rolls or the forefoot leaves the floor.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Supported calf-pop to low knee chamber.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bench","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"ankle","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a free foot/hip turn to produce one modest upward rope pulse.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls. The jump throw explosive power placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not shorten recovery, add fatigue reps, or continue after speed, landing, direction, or release quality declines.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequirements":{"primary_joint_actions":["rotate_pattern_control"],"primary_tissues":["ankle"],"primary_motor_control_demands":["jump_throw_explosive_power"],"breathing_demand":"continuous breathing without bracing or breath-holding drift","balance_demand":"moderate","coordination_demand":"moderate","impact_level":1},"coachingExecution":{"movement_description":"Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a free foot/hip turn to produce one modest upward rope pulse. Coordinate the ankle-led heel release with unloading the free leg, without another landing. Use a smaller heel rise/chamber instead if the ankle rolls or the forefoot leaves the floor.","setup":["Prepare Bench, Marked space; inspect the surface, anchors, clearances, and retrieval path that apply.","Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a free foot/hip turn to produce one modest upward rope pulse."],"execution_steps":["Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a free foot/hip turn to produce one modest upward rope pulse.","Coordinate the ankle-led heel release with unloading the free leg, without another landing.","Use a smaller heel rise/chamber instead if the ankle rolls or the forefoot leaves the floor.","Complete 1 × 2 per support leg = 4 attempts. With fingertip bench support, keep the support knee softly bent and make a brisk heel rise while bringing the opposite bent knee to a low chamber. The supporting forefoot stays down; no hop or large turn. Lower and reset. Rest 20 s between attempts, 60 s between sides/directions, then 60 s before the next entry/section.; preserve the written recovery before repeating."],"coach_cues":["Preserve the named stance, direction, support, and finish.","Full reset; fast and clean, never fatigued."],"athlete_cues":["Fast, clean, then reset.","Stop if the rep changes or symptoms appear."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Shortening recovery and turning quality work into conditioning.","Changing the listed stance, direction, support, landing, or equipment and treating it as the same variation."],"quality_gate":["All prescribed reps match the named setup and finish with stable, repeatable control."],"stop_signs":["Pain, dizziness, unsafe equipment or surface, loss of control, or inability to preserve the named variation."]},"dosage":{"volume_unit":"attempts","default_sets":1,"default_reps":2,"default_work_seconds":null,"default_rest_seconds":20,"est_seconds_per_set":45,"default_rpe_min":7,"default_rpe_max":9},"scaling":{"youth_beginner":"Reduce load, range, speed, distance, impact, and decision demand. Use one coached rep at a time and stop at the first loss of control.","youth_intermediate":"Use the written pattern at a conservative dose; progress one variable only after repeated clean sessions.","teen":"Use the class prescription when readiness and technique support it; keep full recovery for explosive work and clean reps in reserve for strength.","adult_beginner":"Begin below the written load, range, or speed and increase only after the exact start and finish remain repeatable.","adult_advanced":"Use the written variation and progress one measurable constraint at a time without changing the movement identity.","older_adult":"Reduce impact, speed, range, and balance demand; add stable support and longer transitions as needed.","pregnancy_postpartum":"Use an individually cleared lower-impact, lower-load option; avoid breath holding, unstable balance, uncomfortable positions, and symptom-provoking impact."},"genderSpecificNotes":"No default gender-based load split; scale to current technique, training history, symptoms, recovery, and pregnancy/postpartum considerations.","pairsWellAfter":["Prepare & Access movement matching the exercise pattern"],"pairsWellBefore":["Full prescribed recovery before the next output exposure"],"doNotUseWhen":["The exact station, equipment, supervision, or clearance cannot be established.","Pain, dizziness, unusual breathlessness, instability, or a participant request to stop is present.","The athlete cannot preserve the named setup and finish at the planned dose."],"goodForSessions":["athletic_output"],"mediaReferences":["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BZmIA4Sseco","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GoevMondYIs","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9G5Bd_DaP24"],"mediaInternalNotes":["Three embeddable YouTube references are attached. Closest researched movement-family source: Roundhouse kick chamber, pivot, and re-chamber technique (curated YouTube family research (2026-09-14)).","The written card is authoritative for the exact Accelerator stance, direction, support, finish, dose, and safety boundary; do not infer an unshown variation from a video."],"difficultyProfile":{"technical":5,"load":3,"complexity":3,"overall":5,"recommended_age_min":6,"recommended_age_max":null,"attention_demand":"moderate","notes":"Exercise difficulty describes the task; workout readiness remains athlete-specific."},"safety":{"risk_level":1,"impact_level":1,"requires_spotting":false,"requires_coach_supervision":"recommended","readiness_checks":["Confirm the exact station, equipment, surface, clearance, and stop signal.","Confirm the athlete can demonstrate the named start and finish at a lower rehearsal intensity.","Confirm current symptoms, fatigue, and recent workload permit the prescribed exposure."],"contraindications":["Pain, acute injury concern, unsafe equipment or surface, or inability to follow the stop signal."],"common_substitutions":["Use the documented class substitution only after its equipment, dose, duration, and loading