  ('accelerator-supported-fast-lateral-chamber-lift', 'Supported fast lateral chamber lift', '{"slug":"accelerator-supported-fast-lateral-chamber-lift","name":"Supported fast lateral chamber lift","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Chamber → upward hand drive: Keep the supported chamber and band uppercut low enough to preserve a stacked trunk while the limb rises.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Chamber → upward hand drive: Keep the supported chamber and band uppercut low enough to preserve a stacked trunk while the limb rises. Accelerate the thigh into the lateral chamber before the lower leg contributes. Reduce lift height instead if the pelvis hikes or the trunk leans; support must remain light.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Supported fast lateral chamber lift.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bench","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Chamber → upward hand drive: Keep the supported chamber and band uppercut low enough to preserve a stacked trunk while the limb rises.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls. The jump throw explosive power placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accele