  ('accelerator-supported-hip-hike-low-step', 'Supported Hip Hike — low step', '{"slug":"accelerator-supported-hip-hike-low-step","name":"Supported Hip Hike — low step","family":"Joint and tissue resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"slow_eccentric_isometric_joint_resilience","slot":"accelerator_resilience_tissue","cardSummary":"Lightly strengthen pelvic elevation/control over a supported stance hip. Hand support, stance foot on a low stable step, free foot clear. With knee softly straight, lower free-side pelvis slightly for 2 s and return to…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Lightly strengthen pelvic elevation/control over a supported stance hip. Hand support, stance foot on a low stable step, free foot clear. With knee softly straight, lower free-side pelvis slightly for 2 s and return to level for 2 s; do not shrug, bend sideways or push off the free foot. Reduce range for loss of control. If no suitable edge exists, use a supported shallow single-leg squat instead at the same count/tempo to retain stance-pelvis control.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Supported Hip Hike — low step.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Lightly strengthen pelvic elevation/control over a supported stance hip. Hand support, stance foot on a low stable step, free foot clear. W