  ('accelerator-supported-light-dumbbell-forearm-rotation', 'Supported light-dumbbell forearm rotation', '{"slug":"accelerator-supported-light-dumbbell-forearm-rotation","name":"Supported light-dumbbell forearm rotation","family":"Joint and tissue resilience","primaryPhaseKey":"resilience","subrole":"slow_eccentric_isometric_joint_resilience","slot":"accelerator_resilience_tissue","cardSummary":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator resilience block with the listed dose and recovery. Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the drill into conditioning or pre-fatiguing later work.","description":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness. Control the forearm orientation needed for a stable ball/punch wrist. Seated with forearm supported on the thigh and elbow bent, hold a very light dumbbell securely with the wrist straight. Rotate slowly from a comfortable palm-up to palm-down orientation and back; one complete out-and-back is one rep. Use less load or a smaller rotation if the wrist bends or grip strains.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Supported light-dumbbell forearm rotation.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"dumbbell","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"wrist","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Support the shared rotational base with light control work; preserve primary-strength freshness.","whyItGoesHere":"Build control and tissue tolerance without turning the dril