  ('accelerator-supported-low-outward-crescent-sweep', 'Supported low outward crescent sweep', '{"slug":"accelerator-supported-low-outward-crescent-sweep","name":"Supported low outward crescent sweep","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Express a small outward hip sweep and actively arrest and recover the free leg under control.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Express a small outward hip sweep and actively arrest and recover the free leg under control. With light fingertip support, start the low free foot near the midline and sweep it outward in a small arc with a soft knee and comfortable hip turn, then fold the knee and set down. No high lift or forced crossing start. A qualified coach must establish the low noncontact execution. Keep the foot below hip height, support foot turning with the pelvis, knee softly extended and recoil active; no target impact, jump, spin or locked-knee snap. Use instead: a bent-knee outward sweep instead if the longer lever causes groin pull or pelvic lean; do not rotate against a fixed support foot. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Supported low outward crescent sweep.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key