  ('accelerator-supported-rapid-knee-flexion-recoil', 'Supported rapid knee-flexion recoil', '{"slug":"accelerator-supported-rapid-knee-flexion-recoil","name":"Supported rapid knee-flexion recoil","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Leg recoil → compact hand stop: Actively fold the knee after acceleration and stop the hand hook near the midline, using controlled return rather than letting either limb fall.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Leg recoil → compact hand stop: Actively fold the knee after acceleration and stop the hand hook near the midline, using controlled return rather than letting either limb fall. Isolate knee-flexor acceleration for the folding phase of re-chamber without another whole kick. Use a smaller fold instead for hamstring cramp, back arching or hip swing; symptoms end the task.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Supported rapid knee-flexion recoil.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"bench","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Leg recoil → compact hand stop: Actively fold the knee after acceleration and stop the hand hook near the midline, using controlled return rather than letting either limb fall.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or power while fresh, using full reco