  ('accelerator-three-point-start-acceleration-first-two-steps', 'Three-Point Start Acceleration — first two steps', '{"slug":"accelerator-three-point-start-acceleration-first-two-steps","name":"Three-Point Start Acceleration — first two steps","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Main launch task: coordinate release of hand support with the legs'' forward push. Use staggered feet and the hand opposite the front leg on the floor; choose comfortable spacing that allows both feet to push without a…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Main launch task: coordinate release of hand support with the legs'' forward push. Use staggered feet and the hand opposite the front leg on the floor; choose comfortable spacing that allows both feet to push without a cramped crouch. Hold still briefly, then release and drive without twisting. First pair uses controlled fast intent to establish stopping; second pair uses the fastest clean intent that preserves it. No blocks or maximal-load test.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Three-Point Start Acceleration — first two steps.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Main launch task: coordinate release of hand support with the legs''