  ('accelerator-traveling-snap-down-athletic-stick', 'Traveling snap-down → athletic stick', '{"slug":"accelerator-traveling-snap-down-athletic-stick","name":"Traveling snap-down → athletic stick","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Rehearses moving into a balanced athletic landing position and holding it before the sequence shifts toward running and elastic drills.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"Travel forward with a small controlled step or low skip. Reach tall, then quickly organize the arms and hips into an athletic stance. Land or settle quietly on two feet and hold the stick long enough to show balance. Reset fully before traveling into the next repetition.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Traveling snap-down → athletic stick.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"balance","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Rehearses moving into a balanced athletic landing position and holding it before the sequence shifts toward running and elastic drills.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not chase fatigue, force range, or continue through a loss of joint, trunk, landing, or balance control.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—load, range, speed, distance, support, or decision demand—while preserving the named movement identity.","movementRequirements":{"primary_joint_actions":["brace_pattern_control"],"primary_tissues":["full_body"],"primary_motor_control_demands":["integrate"],"breathing_demand":"continuous breathing without bracing or breath-holding drift","balance_demand":"moderate-to-high","coordination_demand":"moderate","impact_level":1},"coachingExecution":{"movement_description":"Travel forward with a small controlled step or low skip. Reach tall, then quickly organize the arms and hips into an athletic stance. Land or settle quietly on two feet and hold the stick long enough to show balance. Reset fully before traveling into the next repetition.","setup":["Mark a clear 10 m lane with room to land and hold.","Begin tall; define the athletic stick as a quiet, balanced stop that the athlete can visibly own."],"execution_steps":["Travel forward with a small controlled step or low skip.","Reach tall, then quickly organize the arms and hips into an athletic stance.","Land or settle quietly on two feet and hold the stick long enough to show balance.","Reset fully before traveling into the next repetition."],"coach_cues":["Reach, snap, stick.","Quiet feet.","Freeze the shape before the next rep."],"athlete_cues":["Land balanced.","Knees follow feet.","Hold, then go."],"breathing_cues":["Breathe continuously; do not hold the breath to force a rep."],"common_faults":["Dropping without first becoming organized.","Landing stiff, narrow or with knees collapsing inward.","Bouncing immediately into the next repetition instead of sticking."],"quality_gate":["Every repetition ends in a stable two-foot position.","The athlete absorbs through a comfortable ankle-knee-hip bend without collapse.","The held finish is quiet and controlled before travel resumes."],"stop_signs":["Pain on landing or deceleration.","Repeated unstable, loud or uncontrolled contacts.","Inabil