  ('accelerator-two-bound-lateral-return-to-starting-leg', 'Two-bound lateral return to starting leg', '{"slug":"accelerator-two-bound-lateral-return-to-starting-leg","name":"Two-bound lateral return to starting leg","family":"Deceleration and change-of-direction output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"deceleration_cod_power","slot":"accelerator_output_deceleration_cod","cardSummary":"Lateral return → rising hand path: Recover support after the linked lateral bounds before using a grounded uppercut to express the turn without added travel.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Lateral return → rising hand path: Recover support after the linked lateral bounds before using a grounded uppercut to express the turn without added travel. Qualify opposite-leg acceptance and pushback needed to recover from lateral displacement. Use instead two separately reset short bounds if immediate return is not proven; same four landings, with extra reset time. Reduce distance for a hard receiving knee.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Two-bound lateral return to starting leg.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Lateral return → rising hand path: Recover support after the linked lateral bounds before using a grounded uppercut to express the turn without added travel.","whyItGoesHere":"Express speed or p