  ('accelerator-two-hand-diagonal-battle-rope-chop-pulse', 'Two-hand diagonal battle-rope chop pulse', '{"slug":"accelerator-two-hand-diagonal-battle-rope-chop-pulse","name":"Two-hand diagonal battle-rope chop pulse","family":"Elastic and plyometric output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"elastic_stiffness_plyometric_rudiments","slot":"accelerator_output_elastic","cardSummary":"Release step → diagonal pull: Push out of the held split stance, then use a settled stance to send rotational force down the rope diagonal.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Release step → diagonal pull: Push out of the held split stance, then use a settled stance to send rotational force down the rope diagonal. Reverse an elevated preload into a brief downward rotational impulse. With a light manageable rope pair, start hands near one shoulder; pivot and drive both ends diagonally toward the opposite hip. Settle the rope completely and reset deliberately before another pulse. Use the stated diagonal band-pull replacement if rope weight or clearance prevents clean speed. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Two-hand diagonal battle-rope chop pulse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"ssc_stiffness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"jump","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"battle_rope","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"wrist","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Release step → diagonal pull: Push out of the held split stance, then use a settled sta