  ('accelerator-two-hand-medicine-ball-backhand-throw', 'Two-hand medicine-ball backhand throw', '{"slug":"accelerator-two-hand-medicine-ball-backhand-throw","name":"Two-hand medicine-ball backhand throw","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Express outward transverse force without relying on elbow extension.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Express outward transverse force without relying on elbow extension. Begin hands across the front of the body near the opposite lower ribs, elbows softly bent. Turn toward the cleared lane and sweep both hands outward at waist-to-chest height into the low target. Reset without receiving a rebound. Use a light grippable ball and a verified low target in a permitted, fully contained release area; keep the entire flight, rebound and roll clear of people. Stay grounded, and do not receive a rebound. Use instead: Shorten the sweep if the ball drags the shoulder behind the torso. Apply this change only to the same remaining combined dose and recovery; it replaces the original execution and adds no extra task or make-up attempts. This replacement uses only the remaining combined dose/rest unless explicitly stated; log changed support, event type, load and added time.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Two-hand medicine-ball backhand throw.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"plyometrics","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readi