  ('accelerator-two-hand-rotational-battle-rope-lift-pulse', 'Two-hand rotational battle-rope lift pulse', '{"slug":"accelerator-two-hand-rotational-battle-rope-lift-pulse","name":"Two-hand rotational battle-rope lift pulse","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a free foot/hip turn to produce one modest upward rope pulse.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a free foot/hip turn to produce one modest upward rope pulse. Primary: create a compact upward rotational impulse and stop it cleanly. Start settled rope ends beside one hip. Pivot feet/hips and drive both hands across toward opposite upper-chest height, producing one brief pulse. Keep elbows soft and ribs down, then settle the rope before resetting. Use the stated low-band speed-lift replacement if rope mass or clearance prevents clean acceleration. Rest 90 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Two-hand rotational battle-rope lift pulse.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"battle_rope","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"wrist","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Heel release → rising impulse: Keep the calf-pop grounded, then use a