  ('accelerator-two-hand-transverse-battle-rope-whip', 'Two-hand transverse battle-rope whip', '{"slug":"accelerator-two-hand-transverse-battle-rope-whip","name":"Two-hand transverse battle-rope whip","family":"Jump, throw, and explosive power","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"jump_throw_explosive_power","slot":"accelerator_output_jump_throw","cardSummary":"Project → arrest the endpoint: Control the broad-jump landing, then stop a single transverse rope impulse from a grounded base; compare endpoint control, not output distances.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Project → arrest the endpoint: Control the broad-jump landing, then stop a single transverse rope impulse from a grounded base; compare endpoint control, not output distances. Apply a brief rotational impulse against rope inertia, then brake. Facing the rope anchor in an athletic stance, hold one rope end in each hand; shift both hands from beside one hip across to the other with a small foot/hip turn. One directed sweep is one rep; settle the rope and walk hands back slowly before the next. Use the stated band-sweep replacement if rope mass or anchor fit prevents a fast controlled impulse. Rest 60 s between side bouts/sets.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Two-hand transverse battle-rope whip.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"battle_rope","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"wrist","weigh