  ('accelerator-two-point-start-two-step-projection', 'Two-point start — two-step projection', '{"slug":"accelerator-two-point-start-two-step-projection","name":"Two-point start — two-step projection","family":"Acceleration and speed output","primaryPhaseKey":"output","subrole":"acceleration_start_speed","slot":"accelerator_output_acceleration","cardSummary":"Primary start anchor: coordinate the first push, reciprocal arm action and the first two ground contacts. Set a comfortable stagger; hold still briefly, then self-start. Push the floor behind you without deliberately…","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator output block with the listed dose and recovery. Express speed or power while fresh, using full recovery and stopping before output quality falls.","description":"Primary start anchor: coordinate the first push, reciprocal arm action and the first two ground contacts. Set a comfortable stagger; hold still briefly, then self-start. Push the floor behind you without deliberately lengthening the stride. First pair uses controlled fast intent to establish the route; remaining pairs use the fastest clean intent that preserves stopping room.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Two-point start — two-step projection.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Make every effort fast and clean; reset fully before the next one.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"explosiveness","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"neural","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"neural_output_readiness","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"brace","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"box","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"full_body","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Primary start anchor: coordinate the first push, reciprocal arm action and the first two ground contacts. Set a comfortable stagger; hold still briefly, then self-start. Push the floor behind you w