  ('accelerator-walking-lunge-rotation-reach', 'Walking lunge + rotation/reach', '{"slug":"accelerator-walking-lunge-rotation-reach","name":"Walking lunge + rotation/reach","family":"Prepare and access","primaryPhaseKey":"prepare_and_access","subrole":"integrate","slot":"accelerator_prepare_integrate","cardSummary":"Moves the athlete through a controlled split stance while coordinating a comfortable reach and trunk turn over a stable base.","bestPlacement":"Use in the Accelerator prepare and access block with the listed dose and recovery. Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue.","description":"Step forward into a comfortable lunge with the whole front foot supported. Settle the pelvis and trunk before rotating and reaching toward the front-leg side. Return the trunk to center, push through the front foot and step into the next lunge. Alternate legs while traveling the full 5 m.","coachLanguage":"This card represents the exact Accelerator-listed identity “Walking lunge + rotation/reach.” Preserve its declared stance, direction, support, landing or receiving condition, and equipment boundary.","athleteLanguage":"Move with control and stop before the position changes.","participantStructure":"individual","tenets":[{"key":"body_control","weight":5}],"methodologies":[{"key":"balance_stability","weight":5}],"physiology":[{"key":"control_stability","weight":5}],"patterns":[{"key":"rotate","weight":5}],"equipment":[{"key":"cones","weight":5}],"body_regions":[{"key":"hip","weight":5}],"whyItWorks":"Moves the athlete through a controlled split stance while coordinating a comfortable reach and trunk turn over a stable base.","whyItGoesHere":"Increase readiness without creating meaningful fatigue. The integrate placement matches this exercise’s dominant job in the written Accelerator class.","commonMisuse":"Do not chase fatigue, force range, or continue through a loss of joint, trunk, landing, or balance control.","scalingGuidance":"Scale one variable at a time—